1
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:07,341
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,793 --> 00:00:09,676
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,297 --> 00:00:12,375
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:12,415 --> 00:00:17,475
 اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:17,839 --> 00:00:18,767
Dear brothers and sisters,

6
00:00:18,807 --> 00:00:20,705
السلام وعليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:30,212
After, a life of hypocrisy of plotting and planning against Rasool Allah ﷺ

8
00:00:31,044 --> 00:00:37,129
Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) was laying down on his deathbed, Rasool Allah ﷺ visited him.

9
00:00:37,285 --> 00:00:39,912
And this is according to Muhammad Bin Is'haq(محمد بن اسحاق).

10
00:00:40,697 --> 00:00:43,925
And Rasool Allah ﷺ when he saw in his face, the signs of death.

11
00:00:44,171 --> 00:00:45,211
 He told him;

12
00:00:45,496 --> 00:00:48,671
اَمَا وَللهِ اِنْ كُنْتُ لَأَنْهَاكَ عَنْ حُبِّ يَهُوْدَ

13
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:54,369
In the name of Allah, I used to warn you from loving the Jews.

14
00:00:55,053 --> 00:00:56,332
So, Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) said;

15
00:00:56,742 --> 00:00:58,648
قَدْ أَبْغَضَهُمْ أَسْعَدْ بِنْ زُرَارَةْ فَمَهَ

16
00:00:58,976 --> 00:01:02,557
As'ad Bin Zurarah(أَسْعَدْ بِنْ زُرَارَةْ), he despised them, and what did that do for him.?

17
00:01:02,581 --> 00:01:08,633
So, until his last moment Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) was still having split loyalties.

18
00:01:09,130 --> 00:01:13,002
And this shows us an important sign of the hypocrites

19
00:01:13,026 --> 00:01:15,953
and that is that they have loyalty to the Kuffar(كُفَّار)

20
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,949
and they have loyalty to the Christians and the Jews.

21
00:01:20,266 --> 00:01:26,164
And this is a sign that has repeated itself in Qur'an, more than once.

22
00:01:26,457 --> 00:01:29,555
فَتَرَى الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ مَرَضٌ يُسَارِعُونَ فِيهِمْ

23
00:01:30,028 --> 00:01:33,583
You see that the ones, who have a disease in their heart, these are the Munafiqeen(منافقين)

24
00:01:33,813 --> 00:01:37,353
they are hasting towards them, towards the disbelievers.

25
00:01:38,048 --> 00:01:44,528
So, the Munafiqeen(منافقين) cannot get this love of the Kuffar(كفار) out of their hearts.

26
00:01:44,681 --> 00:01:48,308
In Sahih Al-Bukhari(صحيح ألبخاري), when Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبدالله بن ابي) passed away,

27
00:01:49,203 --> 00:01:52,875
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to pray on his Janazah(جنازة).

28
00:01:53,294 --> 00:01:57,131
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) came and stood in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ and told him;

29
00:01:57,799 --> 00:02:06,470
يا رسول الله: تُصَلِّيْ عَلَيْهِ وَقَدْ قَالَ فِيْ يَوْمِ كَذَا وَكَذَا، وَقَالَ فِيْ يَوْمِ كَذَا كَذَا وَكَذَا

30
00:02:07,014 --> 00:02:09,288
Are you gonna pray on him when he said;

31
00:02:09,312 --> 00:02:13,698
On such and such day this and that, and he said on this day this and that.?

32
00:02:14,043 --> 00:02:18,062
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is going through the past of Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبدالله بن ابي)

33
00:02:18,102 --> 00:02:24,647
he's reminding Rasool Allah ﷺ with the positions that Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) was taking.

34
00:02:25,127 --> 00:02:27,016
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded back and said;

35
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:29,809
دَعْنِيْ يَا عُمَرْ فَإِنِّيْ بَيْنَ خَيْرَتَيْنِ

36
00:02:30,084 --> 00:02:35,338
 وَلَوْ أَعْلَمْ أَنِّيْ إِنْ زِدْتُّ عَلَى السَبْعِيْنَ غُفِرَ لَه’ لَزِدْتُ

37
00:02:35,615 --> 00:02:37,360
O Umar(عمر) leave me alone.

38
00:02:37,535 --> 00:02:44,398
If I know that if I ask Allah to forgive him more than seventy times, it would be accepted, I would do that.

39
00:02:44,896 --> 00:02:49,044
Rasool Allah ﷺ is referring to the Ayah(آية) verse eighty, Surah At-Taubah(سورة التوبة),

40
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:54,194
اِسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ أَوْ لَا تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ

41
00:02:54,615 --> 00:03:03,137
إِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِينَ مَرَّةً فَلَنْ يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَهُمْ

42
00:03:03,556 --> 00:03:13,682
ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْفَاسِقِينَ۝

43
00:03:14,254 --> 00:03:19,110
Ask forgiveness for them, O Muhammad(محمد) or do not ask forgiveness for them.

44
00:03:19,849 --> 00:03:25,580
If you should ask forgiveness for them 70 times never will Allah forgive them.

45
00:03:26,131 --> 00:03:30,075
That is because they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger

46
00:03:30,275 --> 00:03:33,416
and Allah does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.

47
00:03:34,186 --> 00:03:37,339
So, here you see in the Ayah(آية), Allah saying 70 times.

48
00:03:37,379 --> 00:03:38,706
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

49
00:03:38,821 --> 00:03:42,491
If I know that if I do more than 70, Allah will forgive him, I would do so.

50
00:03:42,855 --> 00:03:50,057
Dear Brothers and Sisters, this shows us a quality in Rasool Allah ﷺ that is striking.

51
00:03:50,326 --> 00:03:55,869
Rasool Allah ﷺ has suffered personally, again and again from Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي)

52
00:03:56,867 --> 00:04:04,802
directly and indirectly the plots and the plans and the deception and the lies of Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) are countless.

53
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:14,253
Nevertheless, Rasool Allah ﷺ is still willing to give him a last chance to pray on his Janazah(جنازة) and to ask Allah, to forgive him.

54
00:04:14,851 --> 00:04:22,809
It shows you, how Rasool Allah ﷺ was willing to go out of his way to give his followers another opportunity.

55
00:04:23,271 --> 00:04:27,910
But then Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية) verse 84, in Surah Taubah(سورة التوبة);

56
00:04:28,203 --> 00:04:37,688
وَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلَىٰ أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ مَاتَ أَبَدًا وَلَا تَقُمْ عَلَىٰ قَبْرِهِ

57
00:04:38,114 --> 00:04:46,103
 إِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ فَاسِقُونَ۝

58
00:04:46,818 --> 00:04:48,069
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

59
00:04:48,191 --> 00:04:55,702
And do not pray over any of them who has died ever, or stand at his grave.

60
00:04:55,932 --> 00:05:00,598
 Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died,

61
00:05:00,946 --> 00:05:02,828
while they were defiantly disobedient.

62
00:05:03,301 --> 00:05:05,633
So, now the issue is clarified

63
00:05:06,028 --> 00:05:10,351
that no Salah(صلاة) should be on offered on the Munafiqeen(منافقين) and this is the final Hukum(حكم),

64
00:05:10,848 --> 00:05:14,200
this is the final judgment on the issue.

65
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:22,036
And this is one of the incidents in which the Qur'an supported the opinion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

66
00:05:22,568 --> 00:05:28,431
It is Hikmah(حكمة) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ that Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) would not survive Muhammadﷺ

67
00:05:28,471 --> 00:05:30,116
and he would actually die before him.

68
00:05:30,252 --> 00:05:34,736
Because Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) was living with hope, with aspirations

69
00:05:34,928 --> 00:05:43,010
that by being patient, and by not facing the Muslims directly, like the Kuffar(كفار) are doing

70
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:45,261
but by choosing the path of Nifaaq(نفاق)

71
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:55,638
he would be able to go through what he perceives as a temporary phase.

72
00:05:56,121 --> 00:06:01,147
And that in the end, he and his people and his ideas would survive.

73
00:06:01,503 --> 00:06:03,854
That's the thinking that they used to have.

74
00:06:04,507 --> 00:06:11,873
That by sitting tight and waiting, they have a chance and that this Islam thing is a temporary thing.

75
00:06:12,050 --> 00:06:17,613
 It's a phase that's going to come and go and people are going to get back to normal.

76
00:06:17,796 --> 00:06:19,393
And he was living with these hopes

77
00:06:19,828 --> 00:06:26,109
especially that he felt that it was Muhammadﷺ, who stripped him, of his power and authority.

78
00:06:26,133 --> 00:06:28,132
Because as it says in the books of Seerah(سيرة),

79
00:06:28,613 --> 00:06:31,769
his people were planning to appoint him as king over them.

80
00:06:32,281 --> 00:06:38,059
And that is when Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) and his plans were shattered.

81
00:06:38,914 --> 00:06:44,023
So, Abdullah Bin Obbaye(عبد الله بن أبي) ended up dying before Rasool Allah ﷺ.

82
00:06:44,472 --> 00:06:47,474
And the religion of Islam survived.

83
00:06:47,995 --> 00:06:52,170
And the way of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) is a way that dies

84
00:06:52,444 --> 00:06:58,996
and they face Allahعَزّوجَلّ on the day of judgment, and have to face His wrath.

85
00:06:59,828 --> 00:07:07,453
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in the ninth year of Hijrah(هجرى) to make Hajj(حج).

86
00:07:07,899 --> 00:07:13,745
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was to lead the delegation of Hajj(حج) not Rasool Allah ﷺ.

87
00:07:14,624 --> 00:07:17,723
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to make Hajj(حج),

88
00:07:18,173 --> 00:07:23,325
while the false gods are lining up around the Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه).

89
00:07:23,746 --> 00:07:30,484
Ya'ani(يعنى) obviously the idols themselves were already destroyed, but the followers are still coming,

90
00:07:31,032 --> 00:07:36,443
because Shirk(شرك) was still surviving in some parts of Arabia.

91
00:07:36,951 --> 00:07:41,531
Plus, they also had the tradition of doing Tawaf(طواف) naked

92
00:07:41,796 --> 00:07:48,899
they used to believe that, because of their sins, because of their impurity they cannot come with these clothes on.

93
00:07:49,221 --> 00:07:50,895
 So, they would take off their clothes

94
00:07:51,524 --> 00:07:54,301
and then borrow some clothes from the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

95
00:07:54,969 --> 00:07:57,770
they used to view them as being special, Al-Humus(ألحمص).

96
00:07:57,976 --> 00:07:59,352
So they will borrow clothes from them.

97
00:07:59,392 --> 00:08:05,249
But some people were not in the position of borrowing, they don't have any money, they don't have any status to borrow

98
00:08:05,274 --> 00:08:08,208
so they would end up making Tawaf(طواف) naked.

99
00:08:08,398 --> 00:08:14,366
So, you had the dual problem of having Mushrikeen(مشركين) and having naked people go around Al-Ka'aba(ألكعبه).

100
00:08:15,441 --> 00:08:23,954
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to attend Al-Hajj(ألحج) while this Munkar(منكر), this evil was going on.

101
00:08:24,718 --> 00:08:29,122
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه led the Muslims in Al-Hajj(ألحج),

102
00:08:29,162 --> 00:08:34,354
it says that they were a few hundred Sahabah(صحابه), who went with him to make Hajj(حج).

103
00:08:35,109 --> 00:08:42,725
And after he left, Rasool Allah ﷺ, received the first part of Surah At-Taubah(سورة التوبة).

104
00:08:43,377 --> 00:08:49,899
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to send these Ayaat(آيات) to Makkah, so that the people would hear them.

105
00:08:50,583 --> 00:08:53,157
So, they said: Shall we send them to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبو بكر ألصديق)?

106
00:08:53,197 --> 00:08:54,649
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No.

107
00:08:54,921 --> 00:09:01,035
only a man from my household should convey these announcements from me.

108
00:09:01,383 --> 00:09:07,500
And he called Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and he told him to go to Makkah, and to announce the following;

109
00:09:07,887 --> 00:09:13,881
لَا يُؤَدِّيْ عَنِّي إِلَّا رَجُلٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَيْتِيْ ثُمَّ دَعَا عَليَّ بِنَ أَبِيْ طَالِبٍ فَقَالْ اُخْرِجْ بِهَذِه الْقِصَّةِ مِنْ صَدْرِ بَرَاءَةَ

110
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:20,789
وَأَذِّنْ فِي النَّاسِ يَوْمِ النَّحَرِ إِذَا اجْتَمَعُوْا بِمِنَى أَلَا إِنَّهُ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجنَّةَ كَافرٌ

111
00:09:21,324 --> 00:09:23,664
وَلَا يَحُجُّ بَعْدَ الْعَامِ مُشْرِكٌ

112
00:09:23,998 --> 00:09:26,212
 وَلَا يَطُوْفُ بِاْلَبَيْتِ عُرْيَانٌ

113
00:09:26,513 --> 00:09:32,115
وَمَنْ كَانَ لَهُ عِنْدَ رَسُوْلِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم عَهْدٌ فَهُوَ لَهُ إِلَى مُدَّتِهِ

114
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:37,866
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب): Go with these verses from Surah Al-Bara'aa(سورة ألبرآءة)

115
00:09:38,526 --> 00:09:43,692
and announce them, to the people, declare them to the people, when they are gathering in Minaa(منى)

116
00:09:43,977 --> 00:09:49,250
and tell them that no, disbeliever shall enter into paradise.

117
00:09:49,918 --> 00:09:54,296
And no polytheist shall make Hajj(حج) after this year.

118
00:09:55,113 --> 00:10:00,845
And no, naked person shall do Tawaf(طواف) around the house of Allah.

119
00:10:01,521 --> 00:10:06,684
And whoever has a contract of security from Rasool Allah ﷺ

120
00:10:06,946 --> 00:10:11,522
then his contract will be fulfilled until the end of its duration.

121
00:10:12,081 --> 00:10:16,168
And then he had to read the Ayaat(آيات) of Surah At-Taubah(سورة التوبة).

122
00:10:16,208 --> 00:10:18,305
We'll just read the first five Ayaat(آيات).

123
00:10:18,770 --> 00:10:31,500
بَرَاءَةٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ إِلَى الَّذِينَ عَاهَدْتُمْ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ۝

124
00:10:32,114 --> 00:10:37,522
This is a declaration of disassociation from Allah and His Messenger

125
00:10:37,784 --> 00:10:41,850
to those with whom you had made a treaty among the polytheists.

126
00:10:42,596 --> 00:10:49,438
Notice that the Surah(سورة) of Bara'aa(برآءة) which is Taubah(ألتوبة) is the only Surah(سورة) in Qur'an that does not start with

127
00:10:49,493 --> 00:10:50,769
 بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝

128
00:10:51,406 --> 00:10:52,612
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ ۝

129
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,501
Includes the name of Allah, the Merciful.

130
00:10:55,134 --> 00:11:01,947
And this is a straightforward declaration of disassociation from the Kuffar(كفار)

131
00:11:02,147 --> 00:11:03,975
and therefore it does not start with

132
00:11:04,015 --> 00:11:05,555
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝

133
00:11:05,907 --> 00:11:09,257
It starts with Bara'aa(برآءة), disassociation.

134
00:11:09,424 --> 00:11:17,293
That's the first word in this Surah(سورة) disavowal, disassociation, being free from them.

135
00:11:17,727 --> 00:11:22,014
This is a declaration of disassociation from Allah and His Messenger

136
00:11:22,039 --> 00:11:25,915
to those with whom you had made the treaty among the polytheists.

137
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:29,871
فَسِيحُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ

138
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:39,976
وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِي اللَّهِ ۙ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ مُخْزِي الْكَافِرِينَ۝

139
00:11:40,570 --> 00:11:45,689
So, travel freely, O disbelievers throughout the land, during four months

140
00:11:46,162 --> 00:11:51,817
but know that you cannot cause failure to Allah and that Allah will disgrace the disbelievers.

141
00:11:51,857 --> 00:11:53,764
 So, they were given four months.

142
00:11:53,987 --> 00:12:04,551
وَأَذَانٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ إِلَى النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْحَجِّ الْأَكْبَرِ أَنَّ اللَّهَ

143
00:12:05,023 --> 00:12:12,434
أَنَّ اللَّهَ بَرِيءٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ ۙ وَرَسُولُهُ ۚ

144
00:12:12,806 --> 00:12:24,405
فَإِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ ۖ وَإِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِي اللَّهِ

145
00:12:24,807 --> 00:12:30,331
وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ۝

146
00:12:30,990 --> 00:12:38,851
And it is an announcement from Allah and His messenger to the people on the day of the greater pilgrimage

147
00:12:39,236 --> 00:12:45,045
that Allah is disassociated from the disbelievers and so is, His Messenger.

148
00:12:45,481 --> 00:12:48,306
So, if you repent, that is best for you.

149
00:12:48,571 --> 00:12:53,387
But if you turn away then know that you will not cause failure to Allah

150
00:12:53,586 --> 00:12:58,428
and give glad tidings to those, who disbelieve, of a painful punishment.

151
00:12:59,303 --> 00:13:08,696
إِلَّا الَّذِينَ عَاهَدْتُمْ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُصُوكُمْ شَيْئًا

152
00:13:08,892 --> 00:13:16,957
ثُمَّ لَمْ يَنْقُصُوكُمْ شَيْئًا وَلَمْ يُظَاهِرُوا عَلَيْكُمْ أَحَدًا

153
00:13:17,235 --> 00:13:23,597
فَأَتِمُّوا إِلَيْهِمْ عَهْدَهُمْ إِلَىٰ مُدَّتِهِمْ

154
00:13:23,858 --> 00:13:28,667
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَّقِينَ۝

155
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:36,668
فَإِذَا انْسَلَخَ الْأَشْهُرُ الْحُرُمُ فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَيْثُ وَجَدْتُمُوهُمْ

156
00:13:36,903 --> 00:13:42,621
وَخُذُوهُمْ وَاحْصُرُوهُمْ وَاقْعُدُوا لَهُمْ كُلَّ مَرْصَدٍ ۚ

157
00:13:42,828 --> 00:13:50,805
فَإِنْ تَابُوا وَأَقَامُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكَاةَ فَخَلُّوا سَبِيلَهُمْ ۚ

158
00:13:51,059 --> 00:13:55,177
إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ۝

159
00:13:55,994 --> 00:14:01,251
Accepted are those, with whom you made a treaty among the polytheists

160
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:08,041
and then they have not been deficient towards you in anything, or supported anyone against you,

161
00:14:08,279 --> 00:14:11,979
so complete for them their treaty until, their term has ended.

162
00:14:12,378 --> 00:14:14,856
Indeed, Allah loves the righteous who fear Him.

163
00:14:15,454 --> 00:14:21,313
And when the sacred months have passed, then kill the polytheists wherever you find them

164
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:27,663
and capture them and besiege them, and sit in, and wait for them at every place of ambush.

165
00:14:28,003 --> 00:14:33,909
But if they should repent, establish prayer and give Zaka'at(زكواة), let them go on their way.

166
00:14:34,077 --> 00:14:36,315
Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.

167
00:14:36,882 --> 00:14:43,049
These are the Ayaat(آيات) and more, that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) announced to the disbelievers

168
00:14:43,295 --> 00:14:46,960
 in the Hajj(حج) of the ninth year of Hijrah(هجرة).

169
00:14:47,866 --> 00:14:52,043
And it was the last year in which the Mushrikeen(مشركين) are going to make Hajj(حج)

170
00:14:52,068 --> 00:15:01,797
and it was the last year, when the traditions and rituals of disbelief are going to be shown in Makkah.

171
00:15:02,405 --> 00:15:03,545
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

172
00:15:03,807 --> 00:15:08,703
إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ۝

173
00:15:09,084 --> 00:15:16,491
وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا۝

174
00:15:16,823 --> 00:15:24,728
فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا۝

175
00:15:24,967 --> 00:15:30,012
When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest and you see

176
00:15:30,454 --> 00:15:35,177
the people entering into the religion of Allah in multitudes

177
00:15:35,638 --> 00:15:40,684
then exalt Him with praise of your Lord and ask forgiveness of Him.

178
00:15:40,876 --> 00:15:43,961
Indeed, He is ever Accepting of repentance.

179
00:15:44,957 --> 00:15:48,525
When the victory of Allah has come and the conquest

180
00:15:48,858 --> 00:15:51,945
 the result of that would be that people will enter into Islam

181
00:15:52,504 --> 00:15:54,655
as it's mentioned in the books of Seerah(سيرة),

182
00:15:54,988 --> 00:16:02,330
that the tribes of Arabia, were watching the conflict between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Quraish(قريش),

183
00:16:02,637 --> 00:16:04,692
and they were waiting to see who will win.

184
00:16:04,931 --> 00:16:11,651
When Rasool Allah ﷺ defeated Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), the Arabs then came in multitudes accepting Islam.

185
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:15,045
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was seen as the religious authority,

186
00:16:15,156 --> 00:16:18,481
they are the keepers of the house of Allah,

187
00:16:19,153 --> 00:16:24,102
they are the ones, who manage the affairs of the people in Hajj(حج) and Umrah(عمره),

188
00:16:24,489 --> 00:16:27,160
they are the ones, who live in Makkah,

189
00:16:27,428 --> 00:16:30,754
and Makkah was the religious center of the Arabs.

190
00:16:31,208 --> 00:16:33,088
So, people used to look up to them.

191
00:16:33,461 --> 00:16:37,962
And when Muhammadﷺ announced the Prophet hood

192
00:16:38,462 --> 00:16:42,232
and the war between him and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) started,

193
00:16:42,676 --> 00:16:47,501
many of them wanted to sit on the sidelines and not take a position

194
00:16:47,911 --> 00:16:50,499
until, they see where this conflict is heading.

195
00:16:50,811 --> 00:16:52,429
After Makkah was opened.

196
00:16:52,691 --> 00:16:54,734
And then pretty soon after that

197
00:16:54,977 --> 00:17:01,245
the tribes around Makkah started accepting Islam such as Hawazin(هوازن) and many of them became Muslim.

198
00:17:01,277 --> 00:17:05,875
And then after that Thaqeef(ثقيف) they also came and accepted Islam

199
00:17:06,397 --> 00:17:10,256
and we talked about how they were besieged in At-Taef(الطائف) and Rasool Allah ﷺ left them.

200
00:17:10,354 --> 00:17:14,123
Eventually they came with their own choice and accepted Islam.

201
00:17:14,647 --> 00:17:21,918
So, you have Quraish(قريش), and Thaqeef(ثقيف), the largest and most important two tribes in the area accepting Islam.

202
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:26,968
 After that, people were just flooding into Madina accepting Islam.

203
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:31,878
So, the ninth year of Hijrah(هجرى) was called Aam-El-Wafood(عام الوفود), the year of delegations.

204
00:17:32,148 --> 00:17:35,757
These tribes would send their representatives to Madina

205
00:17:36,128 --> 00:17:38,972
and they would pledge allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

206
00:17:39,152 --> 00:17:43,098
And this pledge of allegiance, was also a pledge of allegiance to the Islamic State.

207
00:17:43,430 --> 00:17:46,810
And it's not like they're only accepting Islam and then leaving.

208
00:17:46,953 --> 00:17:51,690
No, they are becoming part of the political entity of Madina

209
00:17:52,069 --> 00:17:59,156
because the Bay'ah(بيعة) that they are giving is the Bay'ah(بيعة) to the head of state, Rasool Allah ﷺ.

210
00:17:59,285 --> 00:18:03,025
So, they are accepting his Hukum(حكم), they're accepting his rule.

211
00:18:03,272 --> 00:18:07,914
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) and Ibn Ishaaq(ابن اسحاق) and Al-Waqadi(الواقعدي), they mentioned many delegations.

212
00:18:08,137 --> 00:18:09,743
I will go through some of them.

213
00:18:10,314 --> 00:18:13,013
And we need to keep in mind here that

214
00:18:13,354 --> 00:18:20,179
even though these all became Muslim, and they are counted as Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

215
00:18:20,595 --> 00:18:26,172
but it is considered that whoever became Muslim before the conquest of Makkah

216
00:18:26,512 --> 00:18:30,854
has a higher status than those who became Muslim after the conquest of Makkah.

217
00:18:31,218 --> 00:18:35,850
Why? Because after the conquest of Makkah, it was becoming very clear

218
00:18:36,096 --> 00:18:40,046
that victory in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is for the Muslims,

219
00:18:40,366 --> 00:18:42,933
but the ones, who accepted Islam before that

220
00:18:43,267 --> 00:18:50,594
for them, becoming Muslim was a choice that they would make, and they would know,

221
00:18:50,849 --> 00:18:54,653
that would they would face hardship and would have to make sacrifice.

222
00:18:55,113 --> 00:19:00,175
So the earlier you became Muslim, the more difficult it was.

223
00:19:01,007 --> 00:19:02,719
And that's why Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

224
00:19:02,743 --> 00:19:10,389
لَا يَسْتَوِي مِنْكُمْ مَنْ أَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ وَقَاتَلَ ۚ

225
00:19:10,873 --> 00:19:20,731
أُولَٰئِكَ أَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِنَ الَّذِينَ أَنْفَقُوا مِنْ بَعْدُ وَقَاتَلُوا ۚ

226
00:19:21,104 --> 00:19:25,684
وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنَىٰ ۚ

227
00:19:25,856 --> 00:19:27,702
Allah says in Surah Al-Hadeed(سورة الحديد)

228
00:19:27,789 --> 00:19:32,275
not equal among you are those who spent before the conquest

229
00:19:32,329 --> 00:19:34,210
and this is referring to the conquest of Makkah

230
00:19:34,385 --> 00:19:37,496
and fought and those who did so after it,

231
00:19:37,758 --> 00:19:43,162
those are greater in degree then they who spent afterwards and fought.

232
00:19:43,628 --> 00:19:47,344
The people of Thaqeef(ثقيف), they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they accepted Islam.

233
00:19:47,528 --> 00:19:57,587
And it says in the narration that they tried to negotiate with Rasool Allah ﷺ to leave their major idol for a year.

234
00:19:57,838 --> 00:20:00,521
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused, they said: Then leave it for a month,

235
00:20:00,569 --> 00:20:04,781
because they were worried that the commoners among the people will be shocked

236
00:20:05,082 --> 00:20:12,686
and wouldn't be able to handle seeing their so called God fall down into rubble, fall down into pieces.

237
00:20:12,893 --> 00:20:16,053
So, they wanted to take it slowly with the people, so they said;

238
00:20:16,093 --> 00:20:22,424
We will accept Islam but we don't want our idol to be destroyed except after a year from now

239
00:20:22,655 --> 00:20:25,384
so that we could take it step by step with the people.

240
00:20:25,868 --> 00:20:27,032
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused.

241
00:20:27,056 --> 00:20:28,527
They said: A month! He refused.

242
00:20:28,567 --> 00:20:29,765
A week! He refused.

243
00:20:30,075 --> 00:20:31,907
 A day! He refused.

244
00:20:32,178 --> 00:20:34,923
And they tried their best to negotiate with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

245
00:20:34,947 --> 00:20:38,014
Rasool Ullah made it clear that he's not going to approve such a thing

246
00:20:38,256 --> 00:20:43,226
false god to stay for an additional moment was unacceptable.

247
00:20:43,769 --> 00:20:49,028
So, then they said: If that's the case, then we are not going to bring it down,

248
00:20:49,195 --> 00:20:50,827
send somebody from your end to do it.

249
00:20:51,212 --> 00:20:56,958
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) and Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'ba(مغيرة بن شعبة), who is from Thaqeef(ثقيف).

250
00:20:57,548 --> 00:21:03,648
They both went and people started saying wait for diseases

251
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:07,999
wait for leprosy, wait for…. they are threatening.

252
00:21:08,038 --> 00:21:09,846
They're threatening and they were serious.

253
00:21:09,870 --> 00:21:13,996
They were threatening Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(المغيرة بن شعبة) that the gods will destroy you.

254
00:21:14,493 --> 00:21:20,982
So, it says that he wanted to make fun of this thought of theirs.

255
00:21:21,768 --> 00:21:28,065
So, he struck the idol with his axe and then he pretended that he fell down.

256
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:34,757
So, they all started screaming and shouting, happy that the gods have struck back against Al-Mugheerah Bin Sho'ba(المغيرة بن شعبة).

257
00:21:35,238 --> 00:21:40,210
And then he stood up and said: You are fools, this is nothing but a piece of stone.

258
00:21:40,527 --> 00:21:42,478
And he started breaking it into pieces.

259
00:21:42,502 --> 00:21:46,758
And then we have the delegation that came from Bannu Tamim(بنوتميم)

260
00:21:47,153 --> 00:21:50,800
They came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he gave them the glad tidings.

261
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:52,069
This is in Bukhari(بخاريْ)

262
00:21:52,372 --> 00:21:54,266
اِقْبَلُوا الْبُشْرَى يَا بَنِى تَمِيمٍ

263
00:21:54,387 --> 00:21:57,435
Accept the glad tidings O, Bani Tamim(بني تميم).

264
00:21:57,572 --> 00:21:59,643
قَالُوا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ قَدْ بَشَّرْتَنَا فَأَعْطِنَا

265
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:02,588
O Rasool Ullah: We have heard that now give us,

266
00:22:02,873 --> 00:22:07,690
we don't want good news, we don't want glad tidings, we want you to give us something.

267
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:10,692
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not like that

268
00:22:10,732 --> 00:22:13,841
and then there were people, who came from Yemen.

269
00:22:14,029 --> 00:22:14,881
So, he told them;

270
00:22:14,944 --> 00:22:17,116
اِقْبَلُوا الْبُشْرَى إِذْ لَمْ يَقْبَلْهَا بَنُو تَمِيمٍ

271
00:22:17,392 --> 00:22:22,374
Accept the glad tidings since Bannu Tamim(بنوتميم) did not accept them.

272
00:22:22,574 --> 00:22:24,337
فَقَالُوا قَدْ قَبِلْنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ

273
00:22:24,362 --> 00:22:26,065
We accepted O Rasool Ullah.

274
00:22:26,695 --> 00:22:35,335
Anyway, when a delegation come it is Rasool Allah ﷺ, who would then appoint among them, a leader.

275
00:22:35,850 --> 00:22:39,840
So, when Bannu Tamim(بنوتميم) came, there were two major leaders among them,

276
00:22:39,864 --> 00:22:45,150
one is Al-Akrah Bin Habis(الأَقْرَعَ بْنَ حَابِسٍ) and the other one is Al-QahQah Bin Ma'bad Bin Zararah(الْقَعْقَاعَ بْنَ مَعْبَدِ بْنِ زُرَارَةَ).

277
00:22:45,818 --> 00:22:47,731
So, it says in Bukhari(بخاريْ) that

278
00:22:47,826 --> 00:22:53,825
Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه suggested to Rasool Allah ﷺ to appoint Al-QahQah Bin Ma'bad(الْقَعْقَاعَ بْنَ مَعْبَدِ) to be their leader.

279
00:22:54,298 --> 00:22:57,631
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: No! Appoint Al-Akrah Bin Habis(الأَقْرَعَ بْنَ حَابِسٍ).

280
00:22:58,159 --> 00:23:02,626
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) became angry and said: You said that only to go against my opinion.

281
00:23:02,973 --> 00:23:03,960
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

282
00:23:03,984 --> 00:23:04,966
مَا أَرَدْتُ خِلاَفَكَ

283
00:23:04,990 --> 00:23:08,048
I did not do that to go against your opinion.

284
00:23:08,171 --> 00:23:13,047
And then, they started arguing with each other and their voices became loud.

285
00:23:13,497 --> 00:23:15,357
And that is when Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية):

286
00:23:15,381 --> 00:23:18,287
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تُقَدِّمُوا بَيْنَ يَدَيِ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ

287
00:23:18,963 --> 00:23:24,816
O, you who have believed! Do not put yourselves before Allah and His Messenger but fear Allah,

288
00:23:24,999 --> 00:23:26,462
indeed Allah is Hearing and Knowing.

289
00:23:26,486 --> 00:23:28,610
This is the first Ayah(آية) in Surah Al-Hujraat(سورة ألحجرات).

290
00:23:29,270 --> 00:23:32,098
And then there's the delegation from Bannu Abd Al-Qais(بنوعبدالقيس),

291
00:23:32,123 --> 00:23:38,016
these are from the extreme eastern part of the Arabian Peninsula.

292
00:23:38,214 --> 00:23:39,704
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

293
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:45,085
آمُرُكُمْ بِأَرْبَعٍ ، وَأَنْهَاكُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ الإِيمَانِ بِاللَّهِ ، هَلْ تَدْرُونَ مَا الإِيمَانُ بِاللَّهِ ؟

294
00:23:45,269 --> 00:23:50,924
شَهَادَةُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ ، وَإِقَامُ الصَّلاَةِ ، وَإِيتَاءُ الزَّكَاةِ ، وَصَوْمُ رَمَضَانَ ، وَأَنْ تُعْطُوا مِنَ المَغَانِمِ الخُمُسَ

295
00:23:51,444 --> 00:23:55,637
وَأَنْهَاكُمْ عَنْ أَرْبَعٍ ، مَا انْتُبِذَ فِي الدُّبَّاءِ ، وَالنَّقِيرِ ، وَالحَنْتَمِ ، وَالمُزَفَّتِ

296
00:23:56,071 --> 00:24:00,473
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I command you with four, and I warn you from four.

297
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:04,664
I command you to believe in Allah and do you know what believe in Allah means.?

298
00:24:05,051 --> 00:24:08,483
To testify that there's no one worthy of worship but Allah

299
00:24:08,507 --> 00:24:15,821
to establish Salah(صلاة), to pay Zakat(زكواة), to fast Ramadhan(رمضان), and to give the one fifth of the booty.

300
00:24:16,104 --> 00:24:19,129
Because they are going to fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

301
00:24:19,547 --> 00:24:23,873
and the rule is that when you gain any spoils of war,

302
00:24:23,897 --> 00:24:28,292
you have to give one fifth of them to the leader.

303
00:24:29,448 --> 00:24:32,205
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ told them: And I warn you from four things.

304
00:24:32,553 --> 00:24:39,496
And these are four different types of containers that they used to use, for drinking their alcohol.

305
00:24:39,859 --> 00:24:43,982
So, they were told not to drink alcohol and also not to use those containers

306
00:24:44,291 --> 00:24:46,521
to get them out of the habit of drinking.

307
00:24:47,056 --> 00:24:51,026
And then there's the incident of Thumamah رضي الله عنه.

308
00:24:51,459 --> 00:24:56,281
Now, this is mentioned among the delegations even though it doesn't belong here.

309
00:24:56,660 --> 00:25:03,176
Because Thumamah(ثمامة), first of all, did not come to Madina by will, but he was arrested and captured.

310
00:25:03,521 --> 00:25:08,269
And second of all, this incident happened before

311
00:25:08,578 --> 00:25:11,729
because Thumamah(ثمامة) is talking about Makkah being Kuffar(كفار) at the time

312
00:25:11,769 --> 00:25:14,549
and now we're talking about a time when Makkah was already Muslim.

313
00:25:14,952 --> 00:25:18,068
But this is where Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), puts it in the sequence

314
00:25:18,092 --> 00:25:22,390
and you would find it in the books of Seerah(سيرة) also within the Aam-El-Wafood(عام الوفود).

315
00:25:22,745 --> 00:25:27,540
Apparently they gathered all of the delegations that would come in one section

316
00:25:27,586 --> 00:25:30,899
even though the timing might not have been the same.

317
00:25:31,656 --> 00:25:34,105
For example, they talk about to Tufail Bin Amr Ad-Doasi(طفيل بن عمرو ألدوسي),

318
00:25:34,422 --> 00:25:37,739
even though he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah not in Madina.

319
00:25:38,172 --> 00:25:41,743
Anyway, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent an army to Najd(نجد)

320
00:25:42,105 --> 00:25:44,425
and they arrested the man from Banni Haneefah(بني حنيفه).

321
00:25:44,449 --> 00:25:48,103
They captured the man from Banni Haneefah(بني حنيفه), his name is to Thumamah Bin Athaal(ثمامة بن أثال).

322
00:25:48,461 --> 00:25:51,223
They bound him to a pillar in the Masjid(مسجد).

323
00:25:51,853 --> 00:25:53,416
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ went to him and said;

324
00:25:53,440 --> 00:25:54,709
مَا عِنْدَكَ يَا ثُمَامَةْ؟

325
00:25:55,166 --> 00:25:56,559
What do you have to say;

326
00:25:57,030 --> 00:25:58,510
 فَقَالَ: عِنْدِيْ خَيْرِ يَا مُحَمَّدْ

327
00:25:58,795 --> 00:26:00,136
I have good to say,

328
00:26:00,492 --> 00:26:02,345
إِنْ تَقْتُلْنِيْ تَقْتُلْ ذَا دَمْ

329
00:26:02,497 --> 00:26:07,871
If you kill me, then you would kill a man, who is very worthy among his people.

330
00:26:07,895 --> 00:26:11,606
I mean, if you do kill me, you would have killed somebody who's important.

331
00:26:12,243 --> 00:26:13,428
That's one interpretation.

332
00:26:13,468 --> 00:26:19,196
The other interpretation it means that you have killed someone who has blood on his hands,

333
00:26:19,385 --> 00:26:22,178
and therefore there's no blame on you, if you do so.

334
00:26:22,506 --> 00:26:24,835
وَإِنْ تُنْعِمْ تُنْعِمْ عَلَى شَاكِرْ،

335
00:26:25,168 --> 00:26:28,759
But if you release me, you would release a person, who's grateful.

336
00:26:29,177 --> 00:26:31,835
وَإِنْ كُنْتَ تُرِيْدَ الْمَالْ، فَسَلْ مِنْه مَا شِئْتَ،

337
00:26:31,859 --> 00:26:34,925
And if you want money, ask me what you want.

338
00:26:35,313 --> 00:26:36,274
Rasool Ullah left him.

339
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:39,481
Then he came to him the next day and said; What do you have to say?

340
00:26:39,732 --> 00:26:40,655
He said the same thing?

341
00:26:40,877 --> 00:26:41,886
عِنْدِيْ مَا قُلْتُ لَكْ

342
00:26:42,375 --> 00:26:43,942
I have, what I already told you.

343
00:26:44,288 --> 00:26:46,925
If you release me, You are releasing a man, who is grateful.

344
00:26:47,562 --> 00:26:52,522
And then he came to him the next day and told him, what do you have to say Thumamah(ثمامة)?

345
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:55,775
He said: I have to say what you already heard.

346
00:26:56,154 --> 00:26:58,112
 فقال : أَطْلِقُوْا ثُمَامَة

347
00:26:58,374 --> 00:27:00,279
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Release him.

348
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:07,880
He left and as soon as he got out of the Masjid(مسجد), he took a Ghusal(غسل), he bathed.

349
00:27:08,245 --> 00:27:10,178
And then he entered in the Masjid(مسجد) and said;

350
00:27:10,202 --> 00:27:13,454
أشهد أن لا إله إلا الله، وأشهد أن محمد رسول الله،

351
00:27:13,974 --> 00:27:18,506
He didn't want to do it when he was tied, but now he's grateful.

352
00:27:18,878 --> 00:27:21,511
And he's free, he could leave if he wants.

353
00:27:21,924 --> 00:27:23,738
But he became Muslim and he said;

354
00:27:23,778 --> 00:27:28,181
 يَا محمد، وَالله مَا كَانَ عَلَى وَجْهِ الْأرْضَ وَجْه أَبْغَضَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ وَجْهِكَ

355
00:27:28,552 --> 00:27:33,135
There was no face on the face of the earth, that was more despised to me than your face.

356
00:27:33,444 --> 00:27:36,149
فَقَدْ أَصْبَحَ وَجْهُكَ أَحَبُّ الْوُجُوْهُ اِلَيْ

357
00:27:36,458 --> 00:27:38,471
Now, your face is the most beloved to me.

358
00:27:39,023 --> 00:27:46,117
وَالله مَا كَانَ مِنْ دِيْنٌ أَبْغَضَ إِلَىَّ مِنْ دِيْنَكْ، فَأَصْبَحَ دِيْنَكْ أَحَبْ الدِّيْنَ إِلَيَّ،

359
00:27:46,621 --> 00:27:50,371
There was no religion that was more despised to me than your religion.

360
00:27:50,524 --> 00:27:53,711
And now your religion has become the most beloved to me.

361
00:27:54,098 --> 00:28:01,119
وَاللهِ مَا كَانَ مِنْ بَلَدِ أَبْغَضَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ بَلَدِكَ، فَأَصْبَحَ بَلَدِكَ أَحَبَّ الْبِلَادِ إِلَيْ،

362
00:28:02,131 --> 00:28:06,554
And there was no land that was more despised to me than your land.

363
00:28:06,801 --> 00:28:09,140
And now your land is the most beloved to me.

364
00:28:09,543 --> 00:28:12,844
وَإنَّ خَيْلَكَ أخَذَتْنِي وأَنَا أُرِيدُ العُمْرَةَ، فَمَاذَا تَرَى؟

365
00:28:13,269 --> 00:28:18,055
And your horsemen have captured me and I wanted to go to Umrah(عمرة),

366
00:28:18,317 --> 00:28:19,691
 what do you think, I should do?

367
00:28:20,050 --> 00:28:24,012
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to go and make Umrah(عمرة).

368
00:28:24,328 --> 00:28:27,360
So, when he arrived to Makkah, they told him.

369
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:27,893
 اصَبَوْتَ

370
00:28:27,917 --> 00:28:29,255
Did you become an apostate?

371
00:28:29,295 --> 00:28:31,231
That's what they would tell people, who become Muslim.

372
00:28:31,408 --> 00:28:31,891
قَالَ: لَا،

373
00:28:31,931 --> 00:28:35,807
No, but I am become Muslim with Muhammadﷺ and then he said;

374
00:28:35,831 --> 00:28:40,402
لَا واللَّهِ، لا تَأْتِيكُمْ مِنَ اليَمَامَةِ حَبَّةُ حِنْطَةٍ، حتَّى يَأْذَنَ فِيهَا النبيُّ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ

375
00:28:40,773 --> 00:28:47,244
And In the name of Allah, not one single grain of wheat would reach you from Yamamah(يمامه)

376
00:28:47,443 --> 00:28:49,427
 until, Rasool Allah ﷺ allows it to you.

377
00:28:49,864 --> 00:28:56,788
And this is an evidence used by those, who accept the procedure of boycotting as a valid weapon of war.

378
00:28:56,923 --> 00:28:58,995
Because Thumamah(ثمامه) what he did.?

379
00:28:59,019 --> 00:29:02,239
Was actually an economical boycott on Makkah

380
00:29:02,340 --> 00:29:05,780
he prevented the caravans from carrying wheat to Makkah.

381
00:29:06,144 --> 00:29:12,816
So, they say that this is evidence boycotting the enemy is a valid way of fighting them.

382
00:29:13,921 --> 00:29:19,252
And then there's a delegation of Bannu Haneefah(بنوحنيفه) which included a man called Musailimah(مسيلمه).

383
00:29:19,701 --> 00:29:25,505
عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ قَالَ: قَدِمَ مُسَيْلِمَةُ الْكَذَّابُ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ  صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ، فَجَعَلَ يَقُولُ

384
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:29,457
إِنْ جَعَلَ لِي مُحَمَّدٌ الْأَمْرَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ اتَّبَعْتُهُ،

385
00:29:29,876 --> 00:29:34,017
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says, that Musaylima(مسيلمه), the liar, came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

386
00:29:34,677 --> 00:29:40,846
and he was saying if Muhammad(محمد) is going to appoint me to lead after him, I would follow him.

387
00:29:41,538 --> 00:29:45,499
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came to him along with Thabit Bin Qais Bin Shammas(ثابت بن قيس بن شماس)

388
00:29:45,523 --> 00:29:51,021
and Rasool Ullah had in his hand a piece of wood from a palm tree, from the leaves of a palm tree.

389
00:29:51,689 --> 00:29:55,091
And then he told Musaylima(مسيلمه) and he's among his people.

390
00:29:55,517 --> 00:29:58,855
لَوْ سَأَلتَنِي هَذِهِ الْقِطْعَةَ مَا أَعْطَيْتُكَهَا

391
00:29:59,243 --> 00:30:01,753
If you ask me to give you this, I wouldn't give it to you.

392
00:30:02,311 --> 00:30:06,085
Let alone giving you the leadership of the Ummah(امة), after me.

393
00:30:06,109 --> 00:30:11,264
I wouldn't even give you this piece of Palm Leave and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

394
00:30:11,289 --> 00:30:13,342
وَلَنْ تَعْدُوَ أَمْرَ اللَّهِ فِيكَ

395
00:30:13,366 --> 00:30:16,559
And you're not gonna surpass, what Allah has destined for you.

396
00:30:17,024 --> 00:30:19,301
وَلَئِنْ أَدْبَرْتَ لَيَعْقِرَنَّكَ اللَّهُ،

397
00:30:19,325 --> 00:30:21,976
And if you leave, Allah will destroy you.

398
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:24,609
وَإِنِّي لَأَرَاكَ الَّذِي أُرِيتُ فِيكَ مَا رَأَيْتُ،

399
00:30:24,917 --> 00:30:29,238
And I think that you are the one, whom I have seen what I saw,

400
00:30:29,262 --> 00:30:32,950
and Rasool Allah ﷺ is referring to a dream that he has seen.

401
00:30:33,356 --> 00:30:35,244
وَهَذَا ثَابِتٌ يُجِيبُكَ عَنِّي

402
00:30:35,506 --> 00:30:38,741
And here is Thabit(ثابت), he will speak to you on my behalf and then Rasool Ullah left.

403
00:30:39,351 --> 00:30:41,259
The dream that Rasool Allah ﷺ is referring to,

404
00:30:41,568 --> 00:30:45,872
بَيْن أنا نائِمٌ رَأَيْتُ في يَدَيَّ سِوارَيْنِ مِن ذَهَبٍ،

405
00:30:46,245 --> 00:30:52,438
فأهَمَّنِي شَأْنُهُما، فَأُوحِيَ إلَيَّ في المَنامِ أنِ انْفُخْهُما، فَنَفَخْتُهُما فَطارا

406
00:30:52,659 --> 00:30:58,351
فأوَّلْتُهُما كَذّابَيْنِ يَخْرُجانِ مِن بَعْدِيْ، أحَدُهُما اَسْوَد اَلْعَنْسِيَّ ، والآخَرُ مُسَيْلِمَةَ

407
00:30:59,082 --> 00:31:01,445
Rasool Allah said صلاوة الله وسلام عليه,

408
00:31:01,485 --> 00:31:08,210
While I was asleep I saw two bracelets from gold on my arms,

409
00:31:08,688 --> 00:31:13,288
 and I was told in my sleep to blow them away.

410
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:16,771
So, I blew them and they flew away.

411
00:31:17,144 --> 00:31:21,996
I interpreted that to mean, two liars who would come after me,

412
00:31:22,218 --> 00:31:25,662
One of them is Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(اَسْوَد اَلْعَنْسِيَّ) and the other one is Musaylima(مسيلمه).

413
00:31:26,170 --> 00:31:30,675
Musaylima(مسيلمه) would later write a letter to Rasool Allah ﷺ and this is in the 11th year of Hijrah(هجرة),

414
00:31:31,015 --> 00:31:35,440
he said: And he sent this letter with, two Messengers that came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ

415
00:31:36,014 --> 00:31:39,767
مِنْ مُسَيْلِمَةَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ، إلَى مُحَمَّدٍ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ

416
00:31:40,295 --> 00:31:44,652
سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ، أَمَّا بَعْدُ، فَإِنِّي قَدْ أُشْرِكْتُ فِي الْأَمْرِ مَعَكَ،

417
00:31:45,018 --> 00:31:52,034
وَإِنَّ لَنَا نِصْفَ الْأَمْرِ ، وَلِقُرَيْشٍ نِصْفَ الْأَمْرِ ، وَلَكِنَّ قُرَيْشًا قَوْمٌ يَعْتَدُونَ

418
00:31:52,502 --> 00:31:57,326
He said: From Musaylim(مسيلمه) The Messenger of Allah, to Muhammad(محمد) the Messenger of Allah

419
00:31:57,862 --> 00:32:04,386
Peace be upon you, I have been involved in the affair with you.

420
00:32:05,015 --> 00:32:12,367
Half of it belongs to us and half of it belongs to Quraish(قريش) but Quraish(قريش) are people who transgress.

421
00:32:13,090 --> 00:32:16,334
So, he's saying that the kingdom needs to be split in half.

422
00:32:17,002 --> 00:32:19,035
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wrote back to him.

423
00:32:19,336 --> 00:32:20,813
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيمِ،

424
00:32:21,278 --> 00:32:24,228
From Muhammad(محمد) the Messenger of Allah to Musaylima(مسيلمه) Al-Kadhhaab(ألكذاب).

425
00:32:24,252 --> 00:32:32,028
السَّلَامُ عَلَى مَنْ اتَّبَعَ الْهُدَى أَمَّا بَعْدُ، فَإِنَّ الْأَرْضَ للَّه يُورَثُهَا مَنْ يُشَاءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ، وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ

426
00:32:32,744 --> 00:32:35,194
Peace be upon those, who follow guidance.

427
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:42,869
The earth belongs to Allah and He will give it to whomever He wills and the end belongs to the righteous.

428
00:32:43,577 --> 00:32:48,836
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ asked them and this is narrated by Abu Dawood Dayalisi(ابوداؤد دعالسي).

429
00:32:48,997 --> 00:32:50,512
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked them;

430
00:32:50,750 --> 00:32:52,434
اَتَشْهَدَانْ اَنِّيْ رَسُوْل الله

431
00:32:52,781 --> 00:32:55,009
Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah,

432
00:32:55,033 --> 00:32:58,768
they said: We testify that Musaylima(مسيلمه) is the Messenger of Allah.

433
00:32:59,132 --> 00:33:00,069
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

434
00:33:00,093 --> 00:33:01,787
آمَنْت بِا للهِ وَرَسُلِه

435
00:33:01,893 --> 00:33:04,258
I believe in Allah and His Messengers.

436
00:33:04,614 --> 00:33:07,125
وَلَوْ كُنْتُ قَاتِلًا رَسُوْلاً لَقَتَلْتُكُمَا

437
00:33:07,473 --> 00:33:11,129
And if I was going to kill a Messenger, I would have killed you.

438
00:33:11,493 --> 00:33:12,568
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said;

439
00:33:12,592 --> 00:33:15,610
فمَضَتِّ السُّنَّةْ اَنْ الرُسُلْ لَا تَقْتُلْ

440
00:33:15,958 --> 00:33:20,326
Abdullah Ibn Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said: It became Sunnah(سنة) that messengers are not killed,

441
00:33:20,768 --> 00:33:25,915
carriers of letters, the messengers in Islam should not be killed.

442
00:33:26,708 --> 00:33:30,775
Even if they are coming from the enemy, even if they are coming from people of war.

443
00:33:30,889 --> 00:33:36,563
As long as they are a messenger, then they are not to be killed, that is the Sunnah(سنة).

444
00:33:36,990 --> 00:33:39,559
And then there's a delegation that came from Najraan(نجران).

445
00:33:39,737 --> 00:33:40,909
And this is a long story.

446
00:33:41,171 --> 00:33:46,310
You could refer to it in the Tafseer(تفسير) of Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) on the Surah(سورة) of Al-Imran(ألعمران).

447
00:33:46,502 --> 00:33:52,792
Because there was a long dialogue that happened and debate about the difference between Christianity and Islam

448
00:33:52,832 --> 00:33:54,694
 and the nature of a Eesa عليه السّلام.

449
00:33:54,948 --> 00:34:01,416
And Rasool Allah ﷺ received the revelation about 80 Ayaat(آيات) from Surah Al-Imran(سورة ألعمران) talking about this,

450
00:34:01,638 --> 00:34:03,671
because the people of Najraan(نجران) were Christian.

451
00:34:04,060 --> 00:34:04,977
Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ) says;

452
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:10,293
جَاءَ العَاقِبُ وَالسَّيِّدُ ، صَاحِبَا نَجْرَانَ ، إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُرِيدَانِ أَنْ يُلاَعِنَاهُ

453
00:34:10,943 --> 00:34:16,255
The Aaqib(عاقب) and the Sayed(سيد) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they wanted to do Mula'ana(ملاعنه).

454
00:34:16,498 --> 00:34:20,304
And this is what is referred to also as Mubahala(مباحله)

455
00:34:20,765 --> 00:34:23,949
where Rasool Allah ﷺ would come out and they would come out

456
00:34:24,289 --> 00:34:29,293
and they would ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to send His wrath and punishment on the liars.

457
00:34:29,977 --> 00:34:33,174
And they refused to do so because they said;

458
00:34:33,214 --> 00:34:38,988
If he is truly a Messenger then that will be the end of us and they refuse and they didn't accept that.

459
00:34:39,281 --> 00:34:44,076
Eventually they have to accept the Hukum(حكم) of Rasool Allah ﷺ even though, they didn't become Muslim.

460
00:34:44,588 --> 00:34:45,894
But they would pay Jizyah(جزيه).

461
00:34:46,116 --> 00:34:46,746
So, they said;

462
00:34:46,770 --> 00:34:52,793
إِنَّا نُعْطِيكَ مَا سَأَلْتَنَا ، وَابْعَثْ مَعَنَا رَجُلًا أَمِينًا ، وَلاَ تَبْعَثْ مَعَنَا إِلَّا رَجُلًا أَمِينًا

463
00:34:52,817 --> 00:34:57,173
They said: Sent with us somebody who's trustworthy, and only send the trustworthy man.

464
00:34:57,521 --> 00:34:58,437
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

465
00:34:58,461 --> 00:35:01,552
لَأَبْعَثَنَّ مَعَكُمْ رَجُلًا أَمِينًا حَقَّ أَمِينٍ ،

466
00:35:02,088 --> 00:35:05,690
I will send with you a man who's truly trustworthy.

467
00:35:06,241 --> 00:35:07,564
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

468
00:35:07,588 --> 00:35:08,758
قُمْ يَا أَبَا عُبَيْدَةَ

469
00:35:09,028 --> 00:35:11,070
Stand up Abu Obaidah(ابو عبيدة).

470
00:35:11,386 --> 00:35:14,025
And this is why Abu Obaidah Amr Bin Jarrah(عُبَيْدَةَ بْنَ الجَرَّاحِ) is called

471
00:35:14,065 --> 00:35:15,264
 أَمِينُ هَذِهِ الأُمَّةِ

472
00:35:15,450 --> 00:35:17,534
The trustworthy man of this Ummah(امة).

473
00:35:18,054 --> 00:35:23,654
And then we have Aamir Bin Tufail(عَامِرِ بْنِ الطُّفَيْلِ) and another man called Rabbad Bin Rabia(أَرْبَدَبن ربيه).

474
00:35:23,797 --> 00:35:25,076
 And these are men from Najd(نجد).

475
00:35:25,494 --> 00:35:28,790
And his people told him and he was a head of his people.

476
00:35:28,814 --> 00:35:32,667
يَا أبا عَامِرُ إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ أَسْلَمُوا فَأَسْلِمْ

477
00:35:33,179 --> 00:35:38,184
They told him: Abu Aamir(ابو عامر) people have become Muslim. Why don't you become Muslim?

478
00:35:38,327 --> 00:35:38,666
He said;

479
00:35:38,700 --> 00:35:40,591
 وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ كُنْتُ آلَيْتُ

480
00:35:40,775 --> 00:35:47,263
أَلَّا أَنْتَهِيَ حتَّى تَتْبَعْ اَلْعَرَبْ عَقْبِيْ، فَأَنَا أَتْبَعُ عَقِبَ هَذَا الْفَتَى مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ؟

481
00:35:47,689 --> 00:35:53,562
He said: I have taken a vow that I would not end, meaning my life would not end

482
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:55,846
until the Arabs Follow me.

483
00:35:55,989 --> 00:35:59,026
 And now you want me to follow this young man from Quraish(قريش).

484
00:35:59,366 --> 00:36:04,198
So, you can see the poisoned minds of these men of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

485
00:36:04,562 --> 00:36:11,580
Where the whole issue of life is seeking power, and greed and authority over others.

486
00:36:11,960 --> 00:36:17,670
So, his whole objective in life is to have the Arabs follow him, walk behind him.

487
00:36:18,307 --> 00:36:23,718
And he doesn't want to become Muslim, because that contradicts with his goal in life.

488
00:36:24,401 --> 00:36:29,140
And people like this do not see the truth and do not follow it.

489
00:36:29,534 --> 00:36:32,817
Because their hearts are too far away from the Fitrah(فطرة).

490
00:36:33,050 --> 00:36:39,650
Their hearts are too attached to false goals of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), which they are chasing like a mirage.

491
00:36:40,506 --> 00:36:45,072
Anyway, they went to Rasool Allah ﷺ, they wanted to strike a deal because they saw that

492
00:36:45,233 --> 00:36:48,551
the Muslims are a force that are to be reckoned with and

493
00:36:48,938 --> 00:36:52,955
if they want to have any authority in the Arabia of the day,

494
00:36:53,201 --> 00:36:55,552
they're going to have to strike a deal with Rasool Allah ﷺ

495
00:36:55,829 --> 00:37:00,504
and they're assuming that Rasool Allah ﷺ is just like them, like their tribal leaders.

496
00:37:00,813 --> 00:37:04,405
So, they want to go and negotiate with him something.

497
00:37:05,003 --> 00:37:09,221
They're not knowing that this is Prophet hood, this is Nabuwwa(نبوة), this is something different.

498
00:37:09,694 --> 00:37:11,220
So, they went to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

499
00:37:11,529 --> 00:37:13,838
فَسَئَلَهْ اَنْ يَجْعَلَ لَهُمْ نِصْفَ الْاَمَرْ

500
00:37:14,045 --> 00:37:16,974
They said: We want you to split the affair between us and you.

501
00:37:17,352 --> 00:37:19,325
فَأَبَى عَلَيْهِمَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ

502
00:37:19,349 --> 00:37:20,674
Rasool Allah ﷺ refused.

503
00:37:21,092 --> 00:37:27,490
فَقَالَ لَه’ عَامِرْ لَعْنَهُ الله أَمَا وَاللَّهِ لَأَمْلَأَنَّهَا عَلَيْكَ خَيْلًا جُرْدًا وَرِجَالً مُرْدًا

504
00:37:27,728 --> 00:37:33,458
In the name of Allah, I'm gonna fill it, meaning Madina, I'm going to fill it, with horses and men.

505
00:37:34,141 --> 00:37:41,378
And he belongs to people, who are numerous, and who are well known as being horsemen

506
00:37:41,734 --> 00:37:43,892
and being good and strong fighters.

507
00:37:43,983 --> 00:37:46,793
So, his threat is not bogus.

508
00:37:47,112 --> 00:37:52,890
I mean, he could truly do that and fill Madina with horses and men

509
00:37:53,402 --> 00:37:54,993
but Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

510
00:37:55,017 --> 00:37:57,939
يَأبى اللهُ عَلَيْكَ ذَالِكْ وَاَبْنَاء الْقَيْلَهْ

511
00:37:58,373 --> 00:38:01,222
Allah would refuse that and the sons of Qayla(قيله),

512
00:38:01,405 --> 00:38:02,698
who are the sons of Qayla(قيله).?

513
00:38:03,214 --> 00:38:07,029
Qayla(قيله) is the mother of the Ansaar(أنْصَار) Al-Aos(الأوس) and Al-Khazraj(الخزرج),

514
00:38:07,053 --> 00:38:11,156
so Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying, Allah refuses that and the sons of Qayla(قيله).

515
00:38:11,839 --> 00:38:15,611
And this shows you the confidence that Rasool Allah ﷺ had in the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

516
00:38:15,989 --> 00:38:20,184
He has tested them and lived with them now, for nine years.

517
00:38:20,382 --> 00:38:25,906
And he has seen their strength and their sacrifice and their willingness to stand with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

518
00:38:26,485 --> 00:38:30,219
Now, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) and Arbad(اربد), they said let's then kill him.

519
00:38:30,762 --> 00:38:33,433
If he refused to negotiate with us, then, let's kill him.

520
00:38:33,956 --> 00:38:37,522
Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) said: I will speak to him and  you come from behind him and strike him with your sword.

521
00:38:37,629 --> 00:38:41,804
So, he would talk to Rasool Allah ﷺ, one narration says,

522
00:38:41,953 --> 00:38:45,969
that the hand of Arbad(اربد) got stuck to the sword, and he couldn't move it,

523
00:38:46,325 --> 00:38:47,695
while the other narration says

524
00:38:48,254 --> 00:38:51,740
that whenever he would try to strike Rasool Allah ﷺ Rasool Ullah would disappear

525
00:38:52,229 --> 00:38:54,618
and he would only see Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) in front of him.

526
00:38:55,513 --> 00:38:57,796
Later on, Abu Aamir(ابوعامر) told him, what's wrong with you?

527
00:38:58,199 --> 00:39:02,704
In the name of Allah, I used to fear no one, as I used to fear you.

528
00:39:03,130 --> 00:39:04,913
And now, I see you as nothing.

529
00:39:05,401 --> 00:39:07,084
Arbad(اربد) told him, what do you want me to do?

530
00:39:07,124 --> 00:39:10,098
Whenever I do tried to strike him, he would disappear.

531
00:39:10,138 --> 00:39:11,957
And you are, the one in front of me.

532
00:39:11,997 --> 00:39:13,235
Did you want me to kill you?

533
00:39:13,628 --> 00:39:15,903
And this is a miracle from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

534
00:39:16,345 --> 00:39:19,351
Anyway, they left with empty hands.

535
00:39:19,855 --> 00:39:24,857
And Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) because of that threat, they made to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

536
00:39:25,103 --> 00:39:28,738
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is the One, Who took care of them.

537
00:39:29,196 --> 00:39:36,685
In the case of Abu Aamir(ابوعامر), on the way he passed by a woman, who belongs to his tribe, and he slept in her house.

538
00:39:37,107 --> 00:39:41,081
By the time he woke up, there was a big swelling in his neck,

539
00:39:41,421 --> 00:39:44,020
some kind of disease afflicted him.

540
00:39:44,273 --> 00:39:46,639
 And it is something that kills.

541
00:39:46,907 --> 00:39:52,113
So he didn't want to die in the house of this woman, even though, he was in extreme pain

542
00:39:52,686 --> 00:39:59,527
he went on his horse, and he just kept on wandering until, he died on his horse back.

543
00:39:59,929 --> 00:40:01,425
And that was the end of him.

544
00:40:01,933 --> 00:40:09,693
And with Arbad(اربد), on the way back he was struck by a lightning that killed him, along with his camel.

545
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:16,291
And they mentioned this as, fulfillment of the Ayah(آية) in Surah Ar-Ra'ad(سورة الرعد),

546
00:40:16,529 --> 00:40:17,767
where Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

547
00:40:17,791 --> 00:40:26,647
هُوَ الَّذِي يُرِيكُمُ الْبَرْقَ خَوْفًا وَطَمَعًا وَيُنْشِئُ السَّحَابَ الثِّقَالَ َ

548
00:40:27,071 --> 00:40:33,159
وَيُسَبِّحُ الرَّعْدُ بِحَمْدِهِ وَالْمَلَائِكَةُ مِنْ خِيفَتِهِ

549
00:40:33,326 --> 00:40:39,310
وَيُرْسِلُ الصَّوَاعِقَ فَيُصِيبُ بِهَا مَنْ يَشَاءُ

550
00:40:39,680 --> 00:40:45,674
وَهُمْ يُجَادِلُونَ فِي اللَّهِ وَهُوَ شَدِيدُ الْمِحَالِ۝

551
00:40:46,124 --> 00:40:51,463
It is He, Who shows you lightning causing fear and aspiration and generates the heavy clouds

552
00:40:51,994 --> 00:40:54,822
 and the thunder exalts Allah with praise of Him

553
00:40:55,279 --> 00:40:57,936
and the angels as well, from fear of Him.

554
00:40:58,261 --> 00:41:02,795
And He sends thunderbolts and strikes there with, whom He wills.

555
00:41:03,049 --> 00:41:06,417
While, they dispute about Allah and He is severe in assault.

556
00:41:07,054 --> 00:41:09,586
And that was the end of these two.

557
00:41:10,255 --> 00:41:15,259
Next delegation: They sent one man as a representative of the tribe

558
00:41:15,536 --> 00:41:18,012
and this man, his name is Zumam Bin Thalibah(ضمام بن ثألبه)

559
00:41:18,586 --> 00:41:23,225
there are quite a few narration, some of them in Bukhari(بخاري) and other Books of Hadith(حديث) of the conversation.

560
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:24,914
There's some difference in wording.

561
00:41:24,954 --> 00:41:28,402
This narration is, the one mentioned by Al-Imam Ahmad(ألإمام أحمد).

562
00:41:28,752 --> 00:41:30,624
It is narrated by Abdullah Ibn Abbas(عبدالله بن عباس).

563
00:41:31,144 --> 00:41:36,374
قَالَ: بَعَثَتْ بَنُو سَعْدِ بْنِ بَكْرٍ ضِمَامَ بْنَ ثَعْلَبَةَ وَافِدًا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ،

564
00:41:36,698 --> 00:41:42,594
Tribe of Bannu Sa'ad Bin Bakr(بنو سعد بن بكر), they sent the Zumam Bin Thalibah(ضمام بن ثألبه) as their representative to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

565
00:41:42,825 --> 00:41:46,031
فَقَدِمَ إِلَيْهِ وَأَنَاخَ بَعِيرَهُ عَلَى بَابِ الْمَسْجِدِ،

566
00:41:46,221 --> 00:41:51,633
ثُمَّ عَلَّقَهُ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ الْمَسْجِدَ وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَالِسٌ فِي أَصْحَابِهِ

567
00:41:52,145 --> 00:41:55,755
So, he came, he tied his camel, then he walked into the Masjid(مسجد)

568
00:41:55,779 --> 00:41:58,260
while Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting with the Sahabah(صحابه).

569
00:41:58,592 --> 00:42:03,057
وَكَانَ ضِمَامٌ رَجُلًا جَلْدًا أَشْعَرَ ذَا غَدِيرَتَيْنِ،

570
00:42:03,451 --> 00:42:09,541
Dhamam(ضمام) was a strong man and he had long hair in two braids.

571
00:42:09,830 --> 00:42:13,755
فَأَقْبَلَ حَتَّى وَقَفَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي أَصْحَابِهِ،

572
00:42:14,064 --> 00:42:16,619
فَقَالَ: أَيُّكُمُ ابْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ؟

573
00:42:16,897 --> 00:42:20,115
So, he said: Who among you is the son of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب)?

574
00:42:20,596 --> 00:42:24,080
And notice here, he didn't say the son of Abdullah(عبدالله), he said the son of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

575
00:42:24,104 --> 00:42:27,873
Because Abdullah(عبدالله) wasn't famous, but Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) was famous all around Arabia.

576
00:42:28,190 --> 00:42:33,608
Remember the important incident of the elephant occurred, when he was the leader of his people.

577
00:42:33,870 --> 00:42:36,632
And he is the one, who went and met with Abrahaa(ابراهة).

578
00:42:36,950 --> 00:42:41,289
So, Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب) had a very high status among the Arabs and he was very well known and famous.

579
00:42:41,419 --> 00:42:43,232
So, he said, Where is the son of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).?

580
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,161
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

581
00:42:44,201 --> 00:42:44,724
 أَنَا

582
00:42:44,798 --> 00:42:46,141
I am the Son of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

583
00:42:46,669 --> 00:42:47,351
قَالَ: مُحَمَّدُ

584
00:42:47,391 --> 00:42:48,866
Are you Muhammad(محمد)? He said: Yes!

585
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:50,427
فقَالَ:ابْنَ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ

586
00:42:50,451 --> 00:42:52,092
You the son of Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب), and then he said;

587
00:42:52,116 --> 00:42:55,674
فقَالَ: يَا ابْنَ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ إِنِّي سَائِلُكَ وَمُغَلِّظٌ عَلَيْكَ فِي الْمَسْأَلَةِ،

588
00:42:55,913 --> 00:42:59,924
He said, I'm going to ask you, and I'm going to be strict in my questions.

589
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:01,900
فَلَا تَجِدَنَّ فِي نَفْسِكَ

590
00:43:01,940 --> 00:43:03,012
So, don't be angry.

591
00:43:03,298 --> 00:43:04,324
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

592
00:43:04,364 --> 00:43:05,474
لَا أَجِدُ فِي نَفْسِي،

593
00:43:05,567 --> 00:43:08,051
I'm not going to be angry, ask whatever you want.

594
00:43:08,075 --> 00:43:13,544
فَسَلْ عَمَّا بَدَا لَكَ ". فَقَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ إِلَهَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكَ،

595
00:43:13,759 --> 00:43:18,740
وَإِلَهَ مَنْ هُوَ كَائِنٌ بَعْدَكَ، آللَّهُ بَعَثَكَ إِلَيْنَا رَسُولًا؟

596
00:43:19,072 --> 00:43:26,655
I ask you in the name of Allah, your God, and the God of the ones, before you and the God of the ones, after you!

597
00:43:26,782 --> 00:43:29,111
 Did he send you as a Messenger?

598
00:43:29,389 --> 00:43:30,448
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

599
00:43:30,488 --> 00:43:31,414
 اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ

600
00:43:31,472 --> 00:43:32,865
Yes! In the name of Allah.

601
00:43:33,130 --> 00:43:40,320
قَالَ: فَأَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ إِلَهَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ كَانَ قَبْلَكَ، وَإِلَهَ مَنْ هُوَ كَائِنٌ بَعْدَكَ،

602
00:43:40,575 --> 00:43:45,753
آللَّهُ أَمَرَكَ أَنَّ تَأْمُرَنَا أَنْ نَعْبُدَهُ وَحْدَهُ، وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئًا

603
00:43:46,059 --> 00:43:50,914
وَأَنْ نَخْلَعَ هَذِهِ الْأَنْدَادَ الَّتِي كَانَ آبَاؤُنَا يَعْبُدُونَ مَعَه’؟

604
00:43:51,192 --> 00:43:52,432
قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ

605
00:43:52,710 --> 00:43:58,218
He said: I asked you in the name of Allah, your Lord and the Lord of the ones before you

606
00:43:58,242 --> 00:44:04,720
and the Lord of the ones after you, did Allah ask you to tell us to worship no one but Him,

607
00:44:04,919 --> 00:44:08,583
and to leave these gods that we use to worship?.

608
00:44:08,728 --> 00:44:10,995
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! In the name of Allah.

609
00:44:11,578 --> 00:44:18,627
He said: Then I asked you in the name of Allah, your Lord and the Lord of the ones before you and the Lord of the ones after you,

610
00:44:19,048 --> 00:44:23,251
did Allah order you that we pray these five daily prayers.

611
00:44:23,275 --> 00:44:25,136
He said: In the name of Allah, Yes!

612
00:44:25,671 --> 00:44:31,872
And then he kept on repeating the same thing with all of the five pillars of Islam.

613
00:44:32,134 --> 00:44:34,990
And Rasool Allah ﷺ will give him the same answer and then he said;

614
00:44:35,306 --> 00:44:41,036
قَالَ: فَإِنِّي أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ، وَأَشْهَدُ أَنَّ سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ،

615
00:44:41,369 --> 00:44:47,321
وَسَأُؤَدِّي هَذِهِ الْفَرَائِضَ، وَأَجْتَنِبُ مَا نَهَيْتَنِي عَنْهُ، ثُمَّ لَا أَزِيدُ وَلَا أَنْقُصُ

616
00:44:47,459 --> 00:44:51,793
He said: I testify that there is no one worthy of worship, but Allah.

617
00:44:51,992 --> 00:44:55,466
And I testify that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

618
00:44:55,710 --> 00:45:02,144
and I am going to fulfill these obligations, and I'm going to leave, what you want me from,

619
00:45:02,523 --> 00:45:05,320
and I'm not gonna add anything or subtract anything.

620
00:45:05,606 --> 00:45:07,489
When he left Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

621
00:45:07,884 --> 00:45:11,133
انْ يَّصْدُقَ ذُو الْعَقِيصَتَيْنِ يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ

622
00:45:11,481 --> 00:45:17,279
If the man with the two braids is true, truthful, then he will enter into paradise.

623
00:45:17,728 --> 00:45:19,711
And then he went on his camel and left.

624
00:45:19,957 --> 00:45:23,486
He went to his people and as soon as he got there, he said;

625
00:45:24,044 --> 00:45:26,297
Al-Laat(الَّات) and Al-Uzzah(العزة) are evil.

626
00:45:26,424 --> 00:45:28,495
They said: What are you saying, O Dhumam(ضمام)?

627
00:45:28,753 --> 00:45:33,098
You will be afflicted with leprosy, or you would become insane.

628
00:45:33,303 --> 00:45:33,573
He said;

629
00:45:33,613 --> 00:45:35,898
 وَيْلَكُمْ، إِنَّهُمَا وَاللَّهِ لَا يَضُرَّانِ

630
00:45:36,216 --> 00:45:39,882
Woe to you, they do not harm and they do not benefit.

631
00:45:40,258 --> 00:45:46,306
Allah has sent the Messenger, and He has revealed to him a book that would save you from what you used to do.

632
00:45:46,607 --> 00:45:51,326
And I testify that there is no God but Allah, and there's no one associated with Him.

633
00:45:51,713 --> 00:45:55,894
And that Muhammad(محمد) is His servant and Messenger and I came to you from him.

634
00:45:56,273 --> 00:45:59,835
And I'm ordering you to do what he ordered me.

635
00:46:00,076 --> 00:46:02,963
And I warned you against the things he warned me from.

636
00:46:03,717 --> 00:46:10,559
By the time that day ended, everyone, men and women in his tribe became Muslim.

637
00:46:10,985 --> 00:46:11,898
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says;

638
00:46:11,938 --> 00:46:18,120
We never know of a delegation that was more blessed for his people than Zumam Bin Thalibah(ضمام بن ثألبه).

639
00:46:18,481 --> 00:46:21,043
And then we have the story of Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم).

640
00:46:21,782 --> 00:46:27,199
Udae Bin Hatim رضي الله عنه, he heard about the Prophet hood of Muhammadﷺ,

641
00:46:27,239 --> 00:46:29,836
he was a Christian and he didn't like it, he wasn't happy with it.

642
00:46:30,051 --> 00:46:34,119
And he was hearing about the expansion of the Islamic State

643
00:46:34,419 --> 00:46:40,706
and that it was reaching closer and closer to his people, the tribe of Ta'ee(طائ) in North East Arabia.

644
00:46:41,343 --> 00:46:45,937
So, he went to the Roman Empire and he said;

645
00:46:46,070 --> 00:46:51,435
When I reached there, I found it, to be worse than my situation back home.

646
00:46:51,460 --> 00:46:56,558
I mean, he was hating staying back home because of the Muslims coming closer and closer.

647
00:46:56,906 --> 00:47:00,812
But then when he went to the Roman Empire, he found it to be even worse, so he came back.

648
00:47:01,340 --> 00:47:03,562
And it says in a one narration

649
00:47:03,586 --> 00:47:06,756
that he told one of the servants to prepare some very strong camels.

650
00:47:07,229 --> 00:47:10,520
And then he said: Whenever you see the banners of the Muslims approaching, Tell me!

651
00:47:11,196 --> 00:47:15,278
So, his servant did see the banners coming, he told him about it.

652
00:47:15,477 --> 00:47:19,415
So, he took his fast camels and ran away,

653
00:47:19,614 --> 00:47:26,049
so the Muslims came and they took his Aunt and in one narration his sister as Prisoners Of War

654
00:47:26,089 --> 00:47:27,813
 and they were brought into Madina.

655
00:47:28,282 --> 00:47:32,018
So, his Aunt total Rasool Allah ﷺ to free her.

656
00:47:32,343 --> 00:47:34,301
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ asked her;

657
00:47:34,411 --> 00:47:36,294
Who are you.? So, she told him.

658
00:47:36,413 --> 00:47:38,532
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told her, you are free.

659
00:47:38,807 --> 00:47:44,064
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told her to ask Rasool Allah ﷺ to provide for you, transportation.

660
00:47:44,326 --> 00:47:47,559
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did so, he was very kind with her.

661
00:47:47,623 --> 00:47:49,480
And she left and she went to Udae(عديئ).

662
00:47:49,684 --> 00:47:51,613
And she told him, what you have done is shameful.

663
00:47:51,637 --> 00:47:53,407
I mean, you ran away and you left your family.

664
00:47:53,711 --> 00:47:56,159
And then she told him, I have come from a man,

665
00:47:56,538 --> 00:48:01,550
who is a Messenger of Allah and he's telling the truth, and she praised Rasool Allah ﷺ.

666
00:48:01,574 --> 00:48:05,666
So, he decided to go and visit him because now he was feeling safe about it.

667
00:48:05,690 --> 00:48:10,127
He was feeling that Rasool Allah ﷺ is somebody you could approach and this is a very important thing,

668
00:48:10,325 --> 00:48:15,015
the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Arabia they would hear false rumors about Rasool Allah ﷺ.

669
00:48:15,474 --> 00:48:18,618
But then when they would hear from people who know him personally

670
00:48:19,001 --> 00:48:22,253
they would see a man, who is merciful and kind and approachable.

671
00:48:22,293 --> 00:48:27,112
 And this encouraged many people to come and meet Rasool Allah ﷺ and see him.

672
00:48:27,614 --> 00:48:32,487
But if it was a man, whom they would fear, or they would feel terrorized from

673
00:48:32,741 --> 00:48:37,440
then this would make them very reluctant to go and visit him.

674
00:48:37,866 --> 00:48:39,138
So, Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم), went.

675
00:48:39,408 --> 00:48:41,298
There are different narrations of what happened

676
00:48:41,322 --> 00:48:45,459
One narration says that when he came in, he had the cross hanging on his chest,

677
00:48:45,483 --> 00:48:47,627
you know the customs of the Christians.

678
00:48:47,947 --> 00:48:49,171
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

679
00:48:49,195 --> 00:48:51,840
اِتَّخَذُوا أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ أَرْبَابًا مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ

680
00:48:52,110 --> 00:48:56,219
They have taken their priests as Gods besides Allah.

681
00:48:56,848 --> 00:49:01,057
Udae(عديئ) assuming that Rasool Allah ﷺ does not understand about Christianity

682
00:49:01,890 --> 00:49:04,053
and that he's the expert since it's his religion.

683
00:49:04,077 --> 00:49:07,335
So, he said: We do not take them as Gods besides Allah.

684
00:49:07,745 --> 00:49:12,444
Rasool Ullah asked him, didn't they make what was Halal(حلال), Haram(حرام), and what was Halal(حلال) Haram(حرام)?

685
00:49:12,468 --> 00:49:14,529
He said: Yes. He said, then you have worshiped them.

686
00:49:15,072 --> 00:49:19,623
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ taught him a meaning of taking them as gods

687
00:49:19,647 --> 00:49:24,289
and that is when you give them the authority to make Halal(حلال), Haram(حرام) and Haram(حرام) Halal(حلال).

688
00:49:24,344 --> 00:49:26,791
Then you have made them as Gods

689
00:49:26,815 --> 00:49:30,587
because this is something that is of the authority of Allah alone.

690
00:49:31,171 --> 00:49:36,006
In another narration Rasool Allah ﷺ told him that,

691
00:49:36,133 --> 00:49:38,200
I understand your religion more than you do.

692
00:49:38,650 --> 00:49:43,673
And he said, so Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) questioned that, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

693
00:49:43,982 --> 00:49:44,911
اَلَسْتَ مِنْ رُكُوْسِيَّ

694
00:49:44,935 --> 00:49:47,979
Don't you belong to the sect of Rukusia(روكوسيا)? He said: Yes!

695
00:49:48,382 --> 00:49:51,593
He said and don't you charge your people Al-Murbaa(ألمربآء)

696
00:49:51,796 --> 00:49:54,775
this is what he would take from them, from their spoils.

697
00:49:54,807 --> 00:49:57,364
He said: Yes! He said: That is not allowed in your religion.

698
00:49:57,790 --> 00:50:00,089
And Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) knew that, that was the case.

699
00:50:00,226 --> 00:50:03,186
He said: As soon as Rasool Allah ﷺ said that I was humbled.

700
00:50:03,635 --> 00:50:04,538
فَتَوَاضَعْتُ لَهَا

701
00:50:05,182 --> 00:50:09,709
In Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ) Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم), he said: We visited Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) in a delegation

702
00:50:09,733 --> 00:50:11,978
فَجَعَل عُمَرُ يَدعُو رَجُلًا رجُلًا ويُسمِّيهم

703
00:50:12,232 --> 00:50:16,341
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would call them one by one and he would name them

704
00:50:16,365 --> 00:50:18,718
meaning that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) knew them all by name.

705
00:50:19,012 --> 00:50:21,429
فَقلتُ أمَا تَعْرِفُنِي يا أَمِيرَ المؤمنين؟

706
00:50:21,746 --> 00:50:26,124
I asked him, Don't you know me? O Ameer Ul Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين), because Umar(عمر) did not call him.

707
00:50:26,522 --> 00:50:26,904
He said:

708
00:50:26,928 --> 00:50:32,042
 بَلَى أسْلَمْتَ إذْ كَفَرُوا، وأَقْبَلْتَ إذْ أدْبَرُوا، ووَفَيْتَ إذْ غَدَرُوا،

709
00:50:32,384 --> 00:50:35,685
وعَرَفْتَ إذْ أنْكَرُوا. فَقالَ عَدِيٌّ، إذًا لَا أُبَالِي

710
00:50:36,093 --> 00:50:40,005
He said: Yes! I know you. You are the one, who became Muslim when they were disbelievers.

711
00:50:40,330 --> 00:50:42,497
And you are the one, who came, when they left,

712
00:50:42,782 --> 00:50:45,996
and you are the one, who fulfilled when they have betrayed

713
00:50:46,283 --> 00:50:49,177
and you are the one, who knew when they have rejected,

714
00:50:49,335 --> 00:50:50,764
you accepted, when they rejected.

715
00:50:51,012 --> 00:50:55,980
Udae(عديئ) said: Then I do not care, as long as you know that about me then I do not care

716
00:50:56,109 --> 00:51:01,827
meaning he was pleased that the Ameer Ul Momineen(امير المؤمنين) knew about him and recognized him.

717
00:51:01,851 --> 00:51:05,348
By the way, Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) was the son of the man

718
00:51:05,610 --> 00:51:10,395
who was the most famous Arab in terms of his generosity Hatim Taaee(حاتم طائ), his father.

719
00:51:10,524 --> 00:51:15,567
There are many tales and legends about the generosity of Hatim Taaee(حاتم طائ).

720
00:51:16,032 --> 00:51:17,094
Udae(عديئ) is his son.

721
00:51:17,347 --> 00:51:19,316
In Al-Bukhari(ألبخاريْ) Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) said;

722
00:51:19,373 --> 00:51:27,408
قَالَ: بَيْنَ أَنَا عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذْ أَتَاهُ رَجُلٌ فَشَكَى إِلَيْهِ الْفَاقَة ثُمَّ وَأَتَاهُ آخر فَشَكَا إِلَيْهِ قَطْعَ الطَّرِيْقْ

723
00:51:27,940 --> 00:51:33,179
Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم), he is a noble man in the society and it comes to Madina

724
00:51:33,553 --> 00:51:36,198
and he sees the situation there.

725
00:51:36,801 --> 00:51:41,387
He was with Rasool Allah ﷺ and a man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, complaining about poverty

726
00:51:41,789 --> 00:51:47,463
and then another man came and complained about bandits, that are preventing the travelers.

727
00:51:47,866 --> 00:51:52,288
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ knowing what Udae(عديئ) is seeing from the situation of Madina.

728
00:51:52,328 --> 00:51:52,747
He told him;

729
00:51:52,771 --> 00:51:55,084
يَا عَدِيَّ هَلْ رَأَيْتَ الْحِيرَةَ

730
00:51:55,447 --> 00:51:56,439
Did you see Al-Heera(الحيره)?

731
00:51:56,479 --> 00:51:59,327
Al-Heera(الحيره) is a city in Iraq.

732
00:51:59,737 --> 00:52:03,078
قُلْتُ: لَمْ أَرَهَا وَقَدْ أُنْبِئْتُ عَنْهَا

733
00:52:03,777 --> 00:52:06,446
I didn't see it, but I have heard about it.

734
00:52:06,739 --> 00:52:13,339
قَالَ: فَإِنْ طَالَتْ بِكَ حَيَاةٌ لَتَرَيَنَّ الظَّعِينَةَ تَرْتَحِلُ مِنَ الْحِيرَةِ حَتَّى تَطُوْفَ بِالْكَعْبَةِ

735
00:52:13,648 --> 00:52:18,060
If you live long enough, you will see a woman traveling from Al-Heera(الحيره),

736
00:52:18,258 --> 00:52:21,905
 until she reaches to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) fearing no one but Allah.

737
00:52:22,507 --> 00:52:26,401
قُلْتُ فِيمَا بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ نَفْسِي: فَأَيْنَ دُعَّارُ طَيِّئٍ

738
00:52:26,710 --> 00:52:29,448
I told myself, I was speaking to myself.

739
00:52:29,815 --> 00:52:32,577
 Where are the Bandits of Taaee(طيئ).?

740
00:52:32,645 --> 00:52:34,229
الَّذِينَ قَدْ سَعَّرُوا الْبِلَادَ؟

741
00:52:34,253 --> 00:52:37,409
The ones, who have turned the land into fire because

742
00:52:38,062 --> 00:52:42,404
traveling from Heera(حيره) to Makkah you have to pass through the land of Udae(عدئ)

743
00:52:42,541 --> 00:52:45,990
and there were many armed robbers and bandits over there

744
00:52:46,307 --> 00:52:48,785
which makes it impossible for a woman to travel.

745
00:52:49,023 --> 00:52:53,094
And now, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that she would travel fearing no one but Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

746
00:52:53,957 --> 00:52:55,317
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

747
00:52:55,389 --> 00:52:59,488
وَلَئِنْ طَالَتْ بِكَ حَيَاةٌ لَتُفْتَحَنَّ كُنُوزُ كِسْرَى

748
00:52:59,646 --> 00:53:02,170
قُلْتُ: كِسْرَى بْنُ هُرْمُزَ؟ قَالَ : كِسْرَى بْنُ هُرْمُزَ

749
00:53:02,485 --> 00:53:08,304
And if you live long enough, the treasures of Kisra(كسرى) will become spoils of war for us.

750
00:53:08,328 --> 00:53:12,934
I said: Kisra(كسرى) the son of Hormuz(هرمز) and this is the Persian Emperor

751
00:53:13,274 --> 00:53:15,718
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Kisra(كسرى) the son of Hormuz(هرمز).

752
00:53:16,269 --> 00:53:23,701
وَلَئِنْ طَالَتْ بِكَ حَيَاةٌ لَتَرَيَنَّ الرَّجُلَ يَخْرُجُ بِمِلْءِ كَفِّهِ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ أَوْ فِضَّةٍ

753
00:53:23,971 --> 00:53:28,344
يَطْلُبُ مَنْ يَقْبَلُهُ مِنْهُ فَلَا يَجِدُ أَحَدًا يَقْبَلُهُ مِنْهُ

754
00:53:28,848 --> 00:53:34,456
And if you live long enough, you would find the man coming with a handful of gold or silver

755
00:53:34,991 --> 00:53:39,706
trying to find somebody, who would accept it from him as Sadaqah(صدقه) and he would find no one.

756
00:53:40,475 --> 00:53:53,278
وَلَيَلْقَيَنَّ اللَّهَ أَحَدُكُمْ يَوْمَ يَلْقَاهُ لَيْسَ بَيْنَهُ وَبَيْنَهُ تُرْجُمَانٌ، يُترجِمُ لَه’: فيقولَنَّ لَه’: أَلَمْ أبعَثْ إليك رسولًا فيُبلِّغَكَ؟! فيقول: بلى

757
00:53:53,302 --> 00:53:54,476
To the end of the hadith(حديث)

758
00:53:55,003 --> 00:53:58,188
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling him about what will happen on the Day of Judgment.

759
00:53:58,213 --> 00:54:00,423
Anyway but Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) said;

760
00:54:00,671 --> 00:54:04,836
Two of the three things that Rasool Allah ﷺ told me, I have seen with my own eyes

761
00:54:04,876 --> 00:54:09,506
and I'm sure that the third one would happen because it was said by Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

762
00:54:10,135 --> 00:54:14,120
In another narration Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم),

763
00:54:14,507 --> 00:54:18,625
probably the reason, why you don't want to follow me is because you see that we are poor.

764
00:54:19,332 --> 00:54:22,736
Many people go by what they see what is apparent,

765
00:54:22,996 --> 00:54:27,211
and they are affected by the material aspects of things.

766
00:54:27,529 --> 00:54:32,096
They see people wealthy if they see them successful, in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) they're impressed with that.

767
00:54:32,421 --> 00:54:34,046
And this is false and this is wrong.

768
00:54:34,227 --> 00:54:41,189
One should look at the spirit, one should look at the at the essence of the message and not at the material things

769
00:54:41,545 --> 00:54:45,422
because Udae Bin Hatim(عديئ بن حاتم) admitted that this is what was turning him away from Islam.

770
00:54:45,446 --> 00:54:47,278
Because he sees that Muslims are poor people,

771
00:54:47,556 --> 00:54:48,968
they don't have nice houses,

772
00:54:49,008 --> 00:54:51,042
they don't have beautiful roads,

773
00:54:51,110 --> 00:54:55,143
they don't have advanced cities, like we have back home.

774
00:54:55,389 --> 00:54:57,639
And this was turning him away from Islam.

775
00:54:57,667 --> 00:54:59,547
 Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling him that

776
00:54:59,611 --> 00:55:04,754
the time will come when we mentioned these things that a woman would travel peacefully

777
00:55:05,069 --> 00:55:06,840
without fearing anybody but Allah,

778
00:55:07,094 --> 00:55:12,109
 and that the treasures of Kisra(كسرى) will be spent in the path of Allah.

779
00:55:12,757 --> 00:55:14,835
And then there was a delegation of Al-Ash'areen(ألأشعرين).

780
00:55:14,859 --> 00:55:18,189
Al-Ash'areen(ألأشعرين) are from an area in western Yemen.

781
00:55:18,714 --> 00:55:21,441
In Tahamah(تهامه) in an area called Zabeed(ذبيد)

782
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:25,061
and they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, in Bukhari(بخاريْ) it says;

783
00:55:25,440 --> 00:55:29,216
عنْ أَبِيْ هُريرَةَ رَضِيَ اللهُ عنه عنَّ النَّبيَّ صلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلم قَالَ:

784
00:55:29,399 --> 00:55:36,827
أَتاكُمْ أهْلُ اليَمَنِ، هُمْ أرَقُّ أفْئِدَةً وأَلْيَنُ قُلُوبًا، الإيمانُ يَمانٍ والحِكْمَةُ يَمانِيَةٌ

785
00:55:37,232 --> 00:55:39,688
When this delegation came to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

786
00:55:39,712 --> 00:55:42,417
Rasool Allah ﷺ said according to the narration of Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ).

787
00:55:42,766 --> 00:55:46,296
The people of Yemen have come to you, they are soft hearted.

788
00:55:46,803 --> 00:55:49,966
Eeman(إيمان) is Yemeni! And wisdom is Yemeni!

789
00:55:50,464 --> 00:55:56,347
And this is the praise that Rasool Allah ﷺ has given to the people of Yemen,

790
00:55:56,742 --> 00:56:00,065
that Eeman(إيمان) and Hikmah(حكمة) are Yemeni.

791
00:56:00,741 --> 00:56:06,097
And this was said, when Abu Musa Al-Ashari(ابو موسى الأشعري) and his people came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

792
00:56:06,765 --> 00:56:10,153
And then there's a delegation from the Kings of Himyar(حمير) which is also in Yemen.

793
00:56:10,680 --> 00:56:11,538
اَنْ اَنَسْ اِبْنِ مَالِكْ

794
00:56:11,578 --> 00:56:14,073
And this is narrated by Abu Dawood(ابو داؤد),

795
00:56:14,097 --> 00:56:22,586
اَنْ مَالِكْ دِيْعَزَنْ أهدى اِلَى رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم حُلَّةْ اَخَذَهَا بِثَلَثَةٍ وَثَلَاثِيْنَ بَعيْرَةْ

796
00:56:23,606 --> 00:56:27,566
The Malik Deeazan(مالك ديعزن) has given a gift to Rasool Allah ﷺ

797
00:56:27,687 --> 00:56:32,592
a garment that cost him 33 camels, very expensive

798
00:56:32,971 --> 00:56:35,762
and Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted this gift from him.

799
00:56:36,540 --> 00:56:41,517
And then Jarrir Bin Abdullah Al-Bajali(جرير بن عبد الله البجلي), he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ

800
00:56:41,795 --> 00:56:44,506
according to the narration of Imam Ahmad(امام احمد), Jarrir(جرير) says;

801
00:56:44,885 --> 00:56:53,321
لَمَّا دَنَوْتُ مِنَ المَدِيْنَةِ، أَنَخْتُ رَاحِلَتِي،ثُمَّ حَلَلْتُ عَيْبَتِي، ثُمَّ لَبِسْتُ حُلَّتِي، ثُمَّ دَخَلْتُ المَسْجِدَ، فَإِذَا بِرَسُوْلِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُ

802
00:56:53,747 --> 00:56:56,142
Jarrir(جرير), he puts his camel next to the Masjid(مسجد)

803
00:56:56,166 --> 00:56:59,152
and then he entered while Rasool Allah ﷺ was speaking, was giving Khutba(خطبة)

804
00:56:59,553 --> 00:57:01,851
and people were staring at me.

805
00:57:02,089 --> 00:57:03,204
Why are they looking at him?

806
00:57:03,284 --> 00:57:05,413
He assumed that the reason is

807
00:57:05,453 --> 00:57:10,806
because Rasool Allah ﷺ must have said something about him before he came in and that was the case

808
00:57:11,140 --> 00:57:13,323
 because he asked someone next to him.

809
00:57:13,772 --> 00:57:16,263
Did Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned me, he said: Yes!

810
00:57:16,408 --> 00:57:18,124
ذَكَرَكَ آنِفًا بِأَحْسَنِ الذِّكْرِ،

811
00:57:18,148 --> 00:57:20,974
Yes he mentioned you with a very good mentioning

812
00:57:21,259 --> 00:57:25,155
while Rasool Allah ﷺ was speaking in his Khutba(خطبة)

813
00:57:25,479 --> 00:57:33,518
he said, now a man will come in from this door and you would see on his face signs of a King.

814
00:57:33,907 --> 00:57:38,908
He was very handsome, and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: you would see on his face signs of the king.

815
00:57:39,186 --> 00:57:39,784
Jarir(جرير) said;

816
00:57:39,808 --> 00:57:41,244
فَحَمِدْتُ اللهَ عزوجل

817
00:57:41,268 --> 00:57:43,413
I praise the Allahعَزّوجَلّ for that.

818
00:57:44,026 --> 00:57:45,003
And Jarir(جرير) says;

819
00:57:45,027 --> 00:57:47,417
مَا حَجَبَ للنَّبِيْ صلى الله عليه وسلم مُنْذُوْ اَسْلَمْ

820
00:57:47,765 --> 00:57:52,547
Never did Rasool Allah ﷺ refuse meeting me after I became Muslim.

821
00:57:52,762 --> 00:57:55,563
وَلَا رَاَنِيْ  اِلَّا تَبَسَّمَ فِيْ وَجْهِيْ

822
00:57:55,587 --> 00:57:58,803
Whenever he would see me, he would smile in my face.

823
00:57:59,174 --> 00:58:01,762
وَلَقَد شَكَوْتُ اِلَيْهِ اَنِّيْ لَاَثْبُتُ عَلَى الْخَيْلْ

824
00:58:01,786 --> 00:58:06,060
And I told him that I cannot stay firm on horses.

825
00:58:06,253 --> 00:58:11,441
فَضَرَبَ بِيَدِهِ فِي صَدْرِي فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ ثَبِّتْهُ وَاجْعَلْهُ هَادِيًا مَهْدِيًّا

826
00:58:11,679 --> 00:58:15,862
He struck me in my chest and said, O Allah, make him firm

827
00:58:16,267 --> 00:58:19,609
and make him a guided man and guide through him.

828
00:58:19,866 --> 00:58:22,660
Jarir(جرير) said: I never fell off a horse after that.

829
00:58:23,094 --> 00:58:25,371
This is how Rasool Allah ﷺ won the hearts of people

830
00:58:25,543 --> 00:58:26,973
he would smile in their faces.

831
00:58:27,060 --> 00:58:30,951
He would meet them, he was close to his followers.

832
00:58:31,466 --> 00:58:38,179
And then you have another son of Kings of Hazaral Maot(حضزالموت) his name is Wael Bin Hujr(وائل بن هجر).

833
00:58:38,539 --> 00:58:43,477
He came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he met Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه,

834
00:58:43,502 --> 00:58:46,100
and Rasool Ullah hosted him and treated him very well.

835
00:58:46,783 --> 00:58:49,160
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him a piece of land.

836
00:58:49,556 --> 00:58:57,023
So, Rasool Ullah wants to show the land the location of the land to him, so he sent Muawiya Ibn Abi Sufiyan(معاويه ابن ابي سفيان) with him.

837
00:58:57,069 --> 00:58:59,595
Muawiya(معاويه) at the time was a young man, unknown,

838
00:58:59,999 --> 00:59:04,952
he was sent with Wael(وائل), to show him the location of the land.

839
00:59:05,495 --> 00:59:09,966
فَأَرْسَلَ مَعِي مُعَاوِيَةَ أَنْ أَعْطِهَا إِيَّاهُ أَوْ قَالَ أَعْلِمْهَا إِيَّاهُ

840
00:59:10,331 --> 00:59:16,055
 قَالَ : فَقَالَ لِي مُعَاوِيَةُ : أَرْدِفْنِي خَلْفَكَ ، فَقُلْتُ : لَا تَكُونُ مِنْ أَرْدَافِ الْمُلُوكِ

841
00:59:16,473 --> 00:59:20,009
So, Muawiya(معاويه) is going with Wael(وائل), to guide him to the land

842
00:59:20,412 --> 00:59:22,415
and Wael(وائل) is riding on his camel

843
00:59:22,439 --> 00:59:25,681
 and Muawiya(معاويه) is walking and he was walking apparently barefoot or something.

844
00:59:26,105 --> 00:59:30,686
And Muawiya(معاويه) told him, I want to ride with you on your camel,

845
00:59:31,167 --> 00:59:38,444
he said: you're not going to ride with a king and he refused to allow him to ride.

846
00:59:38,730 --> 00:59:40,352
In another narration, it says

847
00:59:40,786 --> 00:59:45,993
that Muawiya(معاويه) told him: I want to ride he said: You are not the king to ride with kings.

848
00:59:46,193 --> 00:59:49,622
And then Muawiya(معاويه) told him the ground is very hot.

849
00:59:49,837 --> 00:59:53,334
So, the Wael(وائل) told him: Use the shade of the camel and walk in it.

850
00:59:54,002 --> 00:59:58,131
So, Muawiya(معاويه) obviously, would not forget how badly he was treated.

851
00:59:58,463 --> 01:00:03,493
And days passed by and Muawiya(معاويه) becomes the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims and who visits him.

852
01:00:03,680 --> 01:00:04,562
Wael Bin Hujr(وائل بن هجر).

853
01:00:04,761 --> 01:00:08,989
So, when Wael came in, Muawiya(معاوية) had him, sit with him, next to him,

854
01:00:09,316 --> 01:00:12,805
on his Sareer(سرير), which is the couch of the king

855
01:00:13,508 --> 01:00:17,400
unlike when he wanted to ride the camel, he was not allowed.

856
01:00:17,748 --> 01:00:21,491
And Muawiya(معاويه) reminded him with what happened that day.

857
01:00:21,909 --> 01:00:23,239
Wael(وائل) would later say;

858
01:00:23,263 --> 01:00:25,627
وَدِدْتُ أَنِّي كُنْتُ حَمَلْتُهُ بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ

859
01:00:25,651 --> 01:00:29,537
I wish that I not only had him ride with me on the camel,

860
01:00:29,561 --> 01:00:32,728
but I wish that I would have him ride in front of me.

861
01:00:33,446 --> 01:00:36,716
And Then there's the delegation of Tamim Ad-Daari(تميم الداري).

862
01:00:37,189 --> 01:00:41,388
And I already talked about this in series on the hereafter

863
01:00:41,428 --> 01:00:43,832
 because it's a very long Hadith(حديث) I will not go through it again.

864
01:00:44,106 --> 01:00:48,223
He's the one who reported to Rasool Allah ﷺ the news of meeting Ad-Dajjal(الدجال).

865
01:00:48,622 --> 01:00:50,626
Hadith(حديث) narrated by  Al-Imam Muslim(امام المسلم).

866
01:00:51,481 --> 01:00:59,316
Finally there's the delegation of Al-Asd(الاسد) or a Yemeni tribe that are from the southern part of Arabia.

867
01:00:59,739 --> 01:01:02,819
seven men from Al-Asd(الاسد) came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

868
01:01:03,135 --> 01:01:07,491
By the way, Al-Asd(الاسد) are related to Ansaar(الأنْصَار) because Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار) are descendants of Al-Asd(الاسد)

869
01:01:08,105 --> 01:01:09,866
and they came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

870
01:01:09,891 --> 01:01:13,688
فَلَمَّا دَخَلْنَا عَلَيَّه وَكَلَّمْنَاه فَاَعْجَبَهُمْ مَا رَاَى من سَمْكِنَا وَزِيْنَة

871
01:01:14,262 --> 01:01:19,623
Rasool Ullah was impressed by them by their looks, and their characters, and their demeanor.

872
01:01:20,112 --> 01:01:20,990
فَقَالَ: مَا اَنْتُمْ؟

873
01:01:21,030 --> 01:01:21,923
What are you.?

874
01:01:22,099 --> 01:01:23,145
قُلْنَا مُؤْمِنُوْنْ

875
01:01:23,417 --> 01:01:24,849
We said: We are believers

876
01:01:25,119 --> 01:01:26,758
فَتَبَسَّمَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

877
01:01:26,782 --> 01:01:28,400
Rasool Allah smiled and said;

878
01:01:28,545 --> 01:01:32,514
إِنَّ لِكُلِ قَوْلٍ حَقِيقَةً ، فَمَا حَقِيقَةُ قَوْلِكُمْ وَإِيمَانِكُمُ ؟

879
01:01:32,909 --> 01:01:35,552
There's a reality for everything.

880
01:01:35,653 --> 01:01:38,145
So, what is the reality of your statement and your Eeman(إيمان)?

881
01:01:38,223 --> 01:01:39,544
Because they said they're believers.

882
01:01:39,726 --> 01:01:42,480
So, what is the reality of that, what is the manifestation of that?

883
01:01:43,094 --> 01:01:49,450
 قُلْنَا : خَمْسَ عَشْرَةَ خَصْلَةً ، خَمْسٌ مِنْهَا أَمَرْتَنَا بِهَا رُسُلُكَ أَنْ نُؤْمِنَ بِهَا

884
01:01:49,790 --> 01:01:58,596
وَ خَمْسٌ أَمَرْتَنَا أَنْ نَعْمَلَ بِهَا ، وَخَمْسٌ تَخَلَّقْنَا بِهَا فِي الجَاهِلِيَّةِ ، فَنَحْنُ عَلَيْهَا الآنَ ، إِلا أَنْ تُكْرَهَ مِنْهَا شَيْئاً

885
01:01:58,991 --> 01:02:04,465
15 characteristics five of them were commanded by your Messengers to us,

886
01:02:05,110 --> 01:02:08,639
five of them you have commanded us to do

887
01:02:08,971 --> 01:02:12,932
and five of them were traditions from the time of Jahilliyah(جاهليه),

888
01:02:13,288 --> 01:02:15,143
except if you want us to change them.

889
01:02:15,456 --> 01:02:19,897
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What are the five which my messengers order you.?

890
01:02:20,190 --> 01:02:26,916
قُلْنَا : " أَمَرْتَنَا أَنْ نُؤْمِنْ بِاللهِ ، وَمَلاَئِكَتِهِ ، وَكُتُبِهِ ، وَرُسِلِهِ ، وَالبَعْثِ بَعْدَ المَوْتِ " ،

891
01:02:27,615 --> 01:02:30,569
We are ordered to believe in Allah, His angels, His books,

892
01:02:30,579 --> 01:02:33,908
His Messengers and Resurrection after death.

893
01:02:34,505 --> 01:02:37,902
قَالَ : " وَمَا الخَمْسُ الَّتِي أَمَرْتُكُم أَنْ تَعْمَلُوا بِهَا ؟ "

894
01:02:38,000 --> 01:02:40,981
What are the five commands that I gave you,

895
01:02:41,391 --> 01:02:51,301
قُلْنَا : " أَمَرْتَنَا أَنْ نَقُوْلَ : " لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللهَ ، وَنُقِيْمَ الصَّلاَةَ ، وَنُؤْتِيَ الزَّكَاةَ ، وَنَصُوْمَ رَمَضَانَ ، ونَحُجَّ البَيْتَ الحَرَامِ مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيْلاً "

896
01:02:51,938 --> 01:02:55,641
You order us to say La illaha illallah(لا اله الا الله), and to establish Salah(صلاة)

897
01:02:55,997 --> 01:03:01,689
and to pays Zakah(زكوة) and to fast Ramadan(رمضان) and to make Hajj(حَجْ) for the one, who's capable.

898
01:03:02,373 --> 01:03:05,631
" وَمَا الخَمْسُ الَّتِي تَخَلَّقْتُم بِهَا فِي الجَاهِلِيَّةِ ؟ " ،

899
01:03:05,784 --> 01:03:11,907
And what are the five, which you have made as your character, in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

900
01:03:12,068 --> 01:03:14,040
قَالُوْا :  الشُّكْرُ عِنْدَ الرَّخَاءِ ،

901
01:03:14,254 --> 01:03:15,832
وَ الصَّبْرُ عِنْدَ البَلاَءِ ،

902
01:03:15,992 --> 01:03:17,701
وَالرِّضَى بِمُرِّ القَضَاءِ ،

903
01:03:17,889 --> 01:03:19,850
وَالصِّدْقُ فِي موَاطنِ اللِّقَاءِ ،

904
01:03:19,927 --> 01:03:21,554
وَتَرْكُ الشَّمَاتَةِ بِالأَعْدَاءِ

905
01:03:22,130 --> 01:03:22,871
Again the five,

906
01:03:22,911 --> 01:03:24,308
 اَلشُّكْرُ عِنْدَ الرَّخَاءِ

907
01:03:24,710 --> 01:03:27,053
Being grateful in times of ease.

908
01:03:27,291 --> 01:03:28,758
وَ الصَّبْرُ عِنْدَ البَلاَءِ

909
01:03:29,004 --> 01:03:31,469
And being patient in times of difficulty.

910
01:03:31,809 --> 01:03:33,392
وَالرِّضَى بِمُرِّ القَضَاءِ ،

911
01:03:33,498 --> 01:03:35,523
And to accept destiny.

912
01:03:35,684 --> 01:03:37,628
وَالصِّدْقُ فِي موَاطنِ اللِّقَاءِ ،

913
01:03:37,765 --> 01:03:40,269
And being truthful when the enemies meet.

914
01:03:40,601 --> 01:03:42,563
وَتَرْكُ الشَّمَاتَةِ بِالأَعْدَاءِ

915
01:03:42,794 --> 01:03:46,622
And avoiding malicious joy out of our enemies.

916
01:03:46,712 --> 01:03:51,697
Meaning they do not go to extremes, in making fun of their enemies,

917
01:03:51,803 --> 01:03:53,744
they are decent even with the enemy.

918
01:03:54,374 --> 01:04:00,623
فَقَالَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى الله عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : " حُكَمَاءُ عُلَمَاءُ كَادُوا مِنْ فِقههم أَنْ يَكُوْنُوا أَنْبِيَاءَ "

919
01:04:01,088 --> 01:04:03,445
You are wise and knowledgeable

920
01:04:03,675 --> 01:04:09,342
and you have almost because of your knowledge you have almost become Prophets.

921
01:04:09,664 --> 01:04:12,360
Rasool Allah ﷺ was very impressed by their wisdom.

922
01:04:13,020 --> 01:04:14,428
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

923
01:04:14,698 --> 01:04:18,621
وَأَنَا أَزِيْدُكُم خَمْساً ، فَيتِمُّ لَكُم عِشْرُوْنَ خَصْلَةً

924
01:04:18,937 --> 01:04:23,396
And I will give you five more, so you will have 20 characteristics.

925
01:04:23,743 --> 01:04:25,147
إِنْ كُنْتُمْ كَمَا تَقُوْلُوْنَ ،

926
01:04:25,323 --> 01:04:28,651
If what you're saying is true, if you are like, what you say.

927
01:04:29,288 --> 01:04:31,013
فَلا تَجَمَّعُوا مَا لا تَأْكُلُوْنَ

928
01:04:31,299 --> 01:04:33,697
Do not collect what you will not eat.

929
01:04:33,952 --> 01:04:36,208
وَلا تَبْنُوا مَا لا تَسْكُنُونَ ،

930
01:04:36,587 --> 01:04:39,054
And do not build, what you will not live in,

931
01:04:39,488 --> 01:04:43,249
وَلا تُنَافَسُوا فِي شَيْءٍ أَنْتُم عَنْهُ غَداً تَزُولُونَ

932
01:04:43,440 --> 01:04:47,002
And do not compete in something that you will leave tomorrow,

933
01:04:47,444 --> 01:04:51,423
وَاتَّقُوا اللهَ الذي إِلَيْهِ تُرْجِعُوْنَ وَعَلَيْهِ تُعْرَضُون

934
01:04:51,623 --> 01:04:57,596
And fear Allah, Whom you will return to and Whom you will be presented to.

935
01:04:57,968 --> 01:05:02,101
وَ ارْغَبُوا فِيمَا عليه تَقْدمُونَ ، وَفِيهِ تَخْلُدُونَ

936
01:05:02,207 --> 01:05:06,689
And strive for, what you are facing ahead of you,

937
01:05:07,178 --> 01:05:10,276
and where you will be living forever, meaning, the afterlife.

938
01:05:10,638 --> 01:05:14,765
فَانْصَرَفَ القَوْمُ مِنْ عِنْدِ رَسُوْلِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ، وَحَفِظُوا وَصِيَّتَهُ ، عَمِلُوا بِهَا

939
01:05:14,790 --> 01:05:19,452
And they left and they followed the advice of Rasool Allah صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

940
01:05:20,096 --> 01:05:24,039
We have only covered some of the delegations that came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

941
01:05:24,169 --> 01:05:28,961
So, you can see that it was a busy year, where people are coming and accepting Islam

942
01:05:29,270 --> 01:05:32,707
from the four corners of the Arabian Peninsula.

943
01:05:32,984 --> 01:05:36,677
And this is towards the end of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

944
01:05:37,041 --> 01:05:39,774
He is now witnessing the fruit of his Daw'ah(دعوة).

945
01:05:40,014 --> 01:05:45,186
He is now harvesting the fruit of the seed which he planted in Makkah

946
01:05:45,424 --> 01:05:47,792
in the early days when it was very difficult.

947
01:05:48,165 --> 01:05:54,607
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ is seeing the manifestation of his efforts due to the blessing of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

948
01:05:54,647 --> 01:05:58,059
and the Barakah(بركة) that Allahعَزّوجَلّ has put in his Daw'ah(دعوة).

949
01:05:58,403 --> 01:06:01,804
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

950
01:06:02,168 --> 01:06:04,281
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

